"21:43:19 I: Finished with exitcode 2\n"
msgstr ""
"$ annotate-output make\n"
"21:41:21 I: Started make\n"
"21:41:21 O: gcc -Wall program.c\n"
"21:43:18 E: program.c: Couldn't compile, and took me ages to find out\n"
"21:43:19 E: collect2: ld returned 1 exit status\n"
"21:43:19 E: make: *** [all] Error 1\n"
"21:43:19 I: Finished with exitcode 2\n"

#. type: SH
#: ../scripts/annotate-output.1:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "CAVEATS AND BUGS"
msgstr "VARNINGAR OCH BUGGAR"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/annotate-output.1:72
msgid ""
"Since STDOUT and STDERR are processed in parallel, it can happen that some "
"lines received on STDOUT will show up before later-printed STDERR lines (and"
" vice-versa)."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom STDOUT och STDERR bearbetas parallellt kan vissa rader som tas emot"
" på STDOUT visas före STDERR-rader som skrivits ut senare (och tvärtom)."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/annotate-output.1:77
msgid ""
"This is unfortunately very hard to fix with the current annotation strategy."
"  A fix would involve switching to PTRACE'ing the process.  Giving nice a "
"(much) higher priority over I<program> could however cause this behaviour to"
" show up less frequently."
msgstr ""
"Detta är tyvärr mycket svårt att rätta med den nuvarande "
"anteckningsstrategin. En rättning skulle innebära att processen PTRACE:as. "
"Att ge nice en (mycket) högre prioritet än I<program> kan dock göra att "
"detta beteende uppträder mer sällan."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/annotate-output.1:80
msgid ""
"B<annotate-output> expects I<program> to output (text) lines (as specified "
"by POSIX) to STDOUT and STDERR."
msgstr ""
"B<annotate-output> förväntar sig att I<program> skriver ut textrader enligt "
"POSIX till STDOUT och STDERR."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/annotate-output.1:85
msgid ""
"In particular, it leads to undefined behaviour when lines are printed that "
"contain NUL bytes.  It further may lead to undefined behaviour when lines "
"are printed that contain bytes that do not form valid characters in the "
"current locale."
msgstr ""
"I synnerhet leder det till odefinierat beteende när rader som innehåller "
"NUL-tecken skrivs ut. Det kan vidare leda till odefinierat beteende när "
"rader som innehåller tecken som inte bildar giltiga tecken i den aktuella "
"lokaliseringen skrivs ut."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/annotate-output.1:89
msgid ""
"When an interactive I<program> asks for input, the question might not be "
"shown until after you have answered it.  This will give the impression that "
"I<program> has hung, while it has not."
msgstr ""
"När ett interaktivt I<program> ber om inmatning kan det hända att frågan "
"inte visas förrän du har svarat på den.  Detta kan ge intrycket att "
"I<program> har hängt sig, vilket inte är fallet."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/annotate-output.1:96
msgid ""
"B<annotate-output> is implemented as a script in the Shell Command Language."
" Shells typically set various (shell) variables when started and may set the"
" `export` attribute on some of them. They further initialise (shell) "
"variables from their own environment (as set by the caller of the shell "
"respectively the caller of B<annotate-output>) and set the `export` "
"attribute on them."
msgstr ""
"B<annotate-output> är implementerat som ett skript i Shell Command Language."
" Skal ställer normalt in olika skalvariabler när de startas och kan sätta "
"attributet `export` på vissa av dem. De initierar även skalvariabler från "
"sin egen miljö (såsom den angetts av den som anropar skalet respektive den "
"som anropar B<annotate-output>) och sätter attributet `export` på dem."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/annotate-output.1:100
msgid ""
"It follows from this, that when the caller of B<annotate-output> wants to "
"set the environment (variables) of I<program>, they may get overridden or "
"additional ones may get added by the shell."
msgstr ""
"Av detta följer att när den som anropar B<annotate-output> vill ställa in "
"miljön, det vill säga variablerna, för I<program> kan de åsidosättas eller "
"ytterligare variabler läggas till av skalet."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/annotate-output.1:106
msgid ""
"Further, environment variables are in principle allowed to have names (for "
"example `.`) that are not valid shell variable names. POSIX does not specify"
" whether or not such environment variables are exported to programs invoked "
"from the shell. No assumptions can thus be made on whether such environment "
"variables will be exported correctly or at all to I<program>."
msgstr ""
"Vidare får miljövariabler i princip ha namn, till exempel `.`, som inte är "
"giltiga skalvariabelnamn. POSIX anger inte om sådana miljövariabler "
"exporteras till program som anropas från skalet. Det går därför inte att "
"anta att sådana miljövariabler exporteras korrekt eller alls till "
"I<program>."

