#. type: TH
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "ARCHPATH"
msgstr "ARCHPATH"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:4
msgid ""
"archpath - output arch (tla/Bazaar) archive names, with support for branches"
msgstr "archpath: skriv ut archarkivnamn, tla/Bazaar, med stöd för grenar"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:6
msgid "B<archpath>"
msgstr "B<archpath>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:9
msgid "B<archpath> I<branch>"
msgstr "B<archpath> I<branch>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:12
msgid "B<archpath> I<branch>B<-->I<version>"
msgstr "B<archpath> I<branch>B<-->I<version>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:15
msgid ""
"B<archpath> is intended to be run in an arch (tla or Bazaar) working copy."
msgstr ""
"B<archpath> är avsett att köras i en archarbetskopia, tla eller Bazaar."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:20
msgid ""
"In its simplest usage, B<archpath> with no parameters outputs the package "
"name (archive/category--branch--version) associated with the working copy."
msgstr ""
"Vid den enklaste användningen skriver B<archpath> utan parametrar ut "
"paketnamnet (archive/category--branch--version) som hör till arbetskopian."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:28
msgid ""
"If a parameter is given, it may either be a branch--version, in which case "
"B<archpath> will output a corresponding package name in the current archive "
"and category, or a plain branch name (without \\(oq--\"), in which case "
"B<archpath> will output a corresponding package name in the current archive "
"and category and with the same version as the current working copy."
msgstr ""
"Om en parameter anges kan den antingen vara branch--version, varvid "
"B<archpath> skriver ut motsvarande paketnamn i aktuellt arkiv och kategori, "
"eller ett enkelt grennamn (utan \\(oq--\"), varvid B<archpath> skriver ut "
"motsvarande paketnamn i aktuellt arkiv och kategori med samma version som "
"den aktuella arbetskopian."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:32
msgid ""
"This is useful for branching.  For example, if you're using Bazaar and you "
"want to create a branch for a new feature, you might use a command like "
"this:"
msgstr ""
"Detta är användbart för att skapa grenar. Om du till exempel använder Bazaar"
" och vill skapa en gren för en ny funktion kan du använda ett kommando som "
"detta:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "CW<baz branch $(archpath) $(archpath new-feature)>\n"
msgstr "CW<baz branch $(archpath) $(archpath new-feature)>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:43
msgid ""
"Or if you want to tag your current code onto a \\(oqreleases\\(cq branch as "
"version 1.0, you might use a command like this:"
msgstr ""
"Eller om du vill tagga aktuell kod på grenen \\(oqreleases\\(cq som version "
"1.0 kan du använda ett kommando som detta:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "CW<baz branch $(archpath) $(archpath releases--1.0)>\n"
msgstr "CW<baz branch $(archpath) $(archpath releases--1.0)>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:54
msgid ""
"That's much easier than using \\(oqbaz tree-version\\(cq to look up the "
"package name and manually modifying the result."
msgstr ""
"Det är mycket enklare än att använda \\(oqbaz tree-version\\(cq för att slå "
"upp paketnamnet och ändra resultatet manuellt."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:57
msgid "B<archpath> was written by"
msgstr "B<archpath> skrevs av"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:59
msgid "Colin Watson E<lt>cjwatson@debian.orgE<gt>."
msgstr "Colin Watson E<lt>cjwatson@debian.orgE<gt>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/archpath.1:63
msgid ""
"Like B<archpath>, this manual page is released under the GNU General Public "
"License, version 2 or later."
msgstr ""
"Precis som B<archpath> ges denna manualsida ut under GNU General Public "
"License, version 2 eller senare."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:41
msgid "bts - command-line interface for Debian's Bug Tracking System (BTS)"
msgstr "bts: kommandoradsgränssnitt för Debians felhanteringssystem, BTS"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:219
msgid "Send Bug Change Request"
msgstr "Skicka begäran om ändring av felrapport"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:221
msgid ""
"B<bts> [I<options>] I<command> [B<#>I<comment>] [B<,> I<command> "
"[B<#>I<comment>]] ..."
msgstr ""
"B<bts> [I<options>] I<command> [B<#>I<comment>] [B<,> I<command> "
"[B<#>I<comment>]] ..."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:225
msgid ""
"* Bug State I<command>s: B<done>|B<close>, B<reopen>, B<archive>, "
"B<unarchive>."
msgstr ""
"* Felstatuskommandon: B<done>|B<close>, B<reopen>, B<archive>, B<unarchive>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:228
msgid ""
"* Bug Organisation I<command>s: B<reassign>, B<clone>, B<merge>, "
"B<forcemerge>, B<unmerge>."
msgstr ""
"* Felorganiseringskommandon: B<reassign>, B<clone>, B<merge>, B<forcemerge>,"
" B<unmerge>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:231
msgid ""
"* Metadata I<command>s: B<retitle>, B<summary>, B<severity>, B<forwarded>, "
"B<notforwarded>, B<blocked>, B<unblock>, B<submitter>."
msgstr ""
"* Metadatakommandon: B<retitle>, B<summary>, B<severity>, B<forwarded>, "
"B<notforwarded>, B<blocked>, B<unblock>, B<submitter>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:237
msgid "* Bug Linking I<command>s: B<affects>."
msgstr "* Fellänkningskommandon: B<affects>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:240
msgid ""
"* Version Tracking I<command>s: B<found>, B<notfound>, B<fixed>, "
"B<notfixed>."
msgstr ""
"* Versionsspårningskommandon: B<found>, B<notfound>, B<fixed>, B<notfixed>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:243
msgid "* Tagging I<command>s: B<tags>, B<user>, B<usertags>."
msgstr "* Taggningskommandon: B<tags>, B<user>, B<usertags>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:246
msgid ""
"* Coordination I<command>s: B<owner>, B<noowner>|B<disown>, B<claim>, "
"B<unclaim>."
msgstr ""
"* Samordningskommandon: B<owner>, B<noowner>|B<disown>, B<claim>, "
"B<unclaim>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:249
msgid "* Blast radius control I<command>s: B<package>, B<limit>."
msgstr "* Kommandon för begränsning av påverkan: B<package>, B<limit>."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:255
msgid "Compose Quoted Reply With In-Line Bug Changes"
msgstr "Skriv ett citerat svar med inbäddade feländringar"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:257
msgid ""
"B<bts reply> I<bug-no>[B<#>I<msg-no>] , I<command> [B<#>I<comment>] "
"[I<command> [B<#>I<comment>]]..."
msgstr ""
"B<bts reply> I<bug-no>[B<#>I<msg-no>] , I<command> [B<#>I<comment>] "
"[I<command> [B<#>I<comment>]]..."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:259
msgid "Act on Bugs from MUA or Message Context"
msgstr "Hantera felrapporter från epostprogram eller meddelandekontext"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:261
msgid "B<bts context> , I<commands> ...  < bug-message.eml"
msgstr "B<bts context> , I<commands> ...  < bug-message.eml"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:264
msgid "Read Bugs (Web or E-Mail)"
msgstr "Läs felrapporter (webben eller e-post)"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:266
msgid "B<bts show>|B<bugs> I<bug-selection>..."
msgstr "B<bts show>|B<bugs> I<bug-selection>..."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:269
msgid "Prepare to Work Offline"
msgstr "Förbered för att arbeta utan anslutning"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:271
msgid "B<bts cache>|B<cleancache> I<bug-selection>..."
msgstr "B<bts cache>|B<cleancache> I<bug-selection>..."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:274
msgid "Manage $EMAIL Subscription"
msgstr "Hantera prenumeration för $EMAIL"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:276
msgid "B<bts subscribe>|B<unsubscribe> I<bug-number>"
msgstr "B<bts subscribe>|B<unsubscribe> I<bug-number>"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:279
msgid "Contribute to Spam Fighting"
msgstr "Bidra till kampen mot skräppost"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:281
msgid "B<bts reportspam>|B<spamreport> I<bug-number>..."
msgstr "B<bts reportspam>|B<spamreport> I<bug-number>..."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:283
msgid "Scripting"
msgstr "Skriptning"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:287
msgid "* List matching bug numbers: B<bts select> I<bug-selection>..."
msgstr "* Lista matchande felnummer: B<bts select> I<bug-selection>..."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:290
msgid "* Fetch Live Bug Status: B<bts status> I<bug-number>"
msgstr "* Hämta aktuell felstatus: B<bts status> I<bug-number>"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:293
msgid ""
"* List bugs in local cache (for shell completion): B<bts listcachedbugs>"
msgstr ""
"* Lista felrapporter i lokal cache (för skalets komplettering): B<bts "
"listcachedbugs>"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:299
msgid "About bts(1)"
msgstr "Om bts(1)"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:301
msgid "B<bts> B<version>|B<help>"
msgstr "B<bts> B<version>|B<help>"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:307
msgid "Change bugs"
msgstr "Ändra felrapporter"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:309
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts severity 69042 normal\n"
" $ bts merge 69042 43233\n"
" $ bts retitle 69042 This is a better bug description\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts severity 69042 normal\n"
" $ bts merge 69042 43233\n"
" $ bts retitle 69042 Detta är en bättre beskrivning av felet\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:314
msgid "Many changes at once (new implicit bug syntax)"
msgstr "Många ändringar samtidigt (ny implicit felsyntax)"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:316
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts severity 69042 normal , merge with 43233 , retitle Another title\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts severity 69042 normal , merge with 43233 , retitle Annan titel\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:319
msgid "Many changes at once (classic syntax)"
msgstr "Många ändringar samtidigt (klassisk syntax)"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:321
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts severity 69042 normal , merge it 43233 , retitle it Another title\n"
" $ bts severity 69042 normal , merge -1 43233 , retitle -1 Another title\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts severity 69042 normal , merge it 43233 , retitle it Annan titel\n"
" $ bts severity 69042 normal , merge -1 43233 , retitle -1 Annan titel\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:325
msgid "Read complete bug report discussion"
msgstr "Läs hela diskussionen om felrapporten"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:327
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts show 69042         # in a browser\n"
" $ bts show --mbox 69042  # in a mailreader - all messages\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts show 69042         # i en webbläsare\n"
" $ bts show --mbox 69042  # i en e-postläsare: alla meddelanden\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:331
msgid "List bugs"
msgstr "Lista felrapporter"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:333
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts show wget          # all bugs in a package\n"
" $ bts show from:$EMAIL   # reported by you\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts show wget          # alla felrapporter i ett paket\n"
" $ bts show from:$EMAIL   # rapporterade av dig\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:337
msgid "Read all mails for several bugs"
msgstr "Läs all e-post för flera felrapporter"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:339
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts show --mbox             # in packages maintained by you\n"
" $ bts show --mbox deb@e.mail  # .. or someone else's\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts show --mbox             # i paket som underhålls av dig\n"
" $ bts show --mbox deb@e.mail  # ... eller någon annans\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:342
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts show --mbox src:wget    # in a source package\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts show --mbox src:wget    # i ett källpaket\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:345
msgid "Reply to bug"
msgstr "Svara på felrapport"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:347
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts reply 43233            # reply to bug no. 43233\n"
" $ bts reply 43233 , done     # .. and add pseudoheader to close\n"
" $ bts done 43233 , reply     # .. other way around also works\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts reply 43233            # svara på felrapport nr. 43233\n"
" $ bts reply 43233 , done     # ... och lägg till pseudohuvud för att stänga\n"
" $ bts done 43233 , reply     # ... det omvända fungerar också\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:351
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # Quote a message\n"
" $ bts reply 43233#15         # reply to bug no. 43233 quoting message 15\n"
" $ bts reply 43233#15 , done  # .. and add Control: pseudoheader to close\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # Citera ett meddelande\n"
" $ bts reply 43233#15         # svara på felrapport nr. 43233 och citera meddelande 15\n"
" $ bts reply 43233#15 , done  # ... och lägg till Control:-pseudohuvud för att stänga\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:356
msgid "Reply to bug on stdin, i.e. from command-line mailreader (MUA)"
msgstr ""
"Svara på felrapport via standardinmatning, det vill säga från en "
"e-postläsare för kommandoraden (MUA)"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:358
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" | bts reply -                  # reply and quote piped bug message\n"
" | bts reply - , close          #.. and close bug\n"
" | bts severity normal , close  #.. 'reply -' is implied inside supported MUA\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" | bts reply -                  # svara och citera rörledningsmatat felmeddelande\n"
" | bts reply - , close          # ... och stäng felrapporten\n"
" | bts severity normal , close  # ... 'reply -' används underförstått i MUA:er som stöds\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:362
msgid ""
"Hint: C<|> indicates to run from (neo)mutt <B<pipe-entry>> command (\"B<|>\""
" key)."
msgstr ""
"Tips: C<|> anger att kommandot körs från (neo)mutts kommando <B<pipe-entry>>"
" (tangenten ”B<|>”)."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:365
msgid "Change bug from command-line mailreader"
msgstr "Ändra felrapport från e-postläsare för kommandoraden"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:367
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" | bts context , retitle 'flub: Does not nub!' , reassign flub\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" | bts context , retitle 'flub: Does not nub!' , reassign flub\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:370
msgid "Show Bug selected from command-line mailreader"
msgstr "Visa felrapport som valts från e-postläsare för kommandoraden"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:372
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" | bts context , status\n"
" | bts context , show\n"
" | bts show                 # 'context' is implied in supported MUA\n"
" | bts subscribe\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" | bts context , status\n"
" | bts context , show\n"
" | bts show                 # 'context' is implied in supported MUA\n"
" | bts subscribe\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:377
msgid ""
"Hint: selecting several bugs/messages (<tag-prefix><pipe-message> in "
"(neo)mutt) is supported for (only) some commands. See L</COMMANDS>."
msgstr ""
"Tips: att välja flera felrapporter/meddelanden (<tag-prefix><pipe-message> i"
" (neo)mutt) stöds för vissa kommandon. Se L</COMMANDS>."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:381
msgid "Subscribe $EMAIL to a bug:"
msgstr "Prenumerera med $EMAIL på en felrapport:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:383
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts subscribe 69042\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts subscribe 69042\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:386
msgid "List selected bugs - for scripting:"
msgstr "Lista valda felrapporter för skriptning:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:388
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bugs=$(bts select src:libc6)\n"
" $ for bug in $bugs; do echo $bug needs fixing; done\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bugs=$(bts select src:libc6)\n"
" $ for bug in $bugs; do echo $bug needs fixing; done\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:396
msgid ""
"B<bts> is the command-line interface for Debian's Bug Tracking System (BTS)."
" It is intended for use by Debian contributors and if you're reading this "
"that means I<*you*>."
msgstr ""
"B<bts> är kommandoradsgränssnittet för Debians Bug Tracking System (BTS). "
"Det är avsett för Debian-bidragsgivare, och om du läser detta betyder det "
"I<*dig*>."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:400
msgid ""
"B<bts> helps make the many common tasks involving bugs in Debian more "
"convenien and enhances your workflow with offline capabilities through local"
" caching."
msgstr ""
"B<bts> förenklar de många vanliga uppgifterna kring felrapporter i Debian "
"och förbättrar arbetsflödet med funktioner för offlinearbete genom lokal "
"cachelagring."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:405
msgid "Contributing to Bugs"
msgstr "Bidra till felrapporter"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:407
msgid ""
"Debian invites I<everyone> to contribute by reporting, analyzing, replying "
"to and triaging bugs -- without the need for permission or so much as an "
"account."
msgstr ""
"Debian uppmuntrar I<alla> att bidra genom att rapportera, analysera, svara "
"på och triagera felrapporter. Det kräver varken tillstånd eller ens ett "
"konto."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:411
msgid ""
"A standard e-mail address (see I<$EMAIL>) and a willingness to learn and "
"collaborate is all that's needed to participate."
msgstr ""
"En vanlig e-postadress (se I<$EMAIL>) och en vilja att lära sig och "
"samarbeta är allt som behövs för att delta."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:414
msgid ""
"That being said we ask you to use B<bts> and the BTS in general responsibly."
" Start by subscribing to packages (pts-subscribe(1)) or particular bugs of "
"interest to you (\"bts subscribe 69042\"). Try to observe other Debian "
"contributors' working conventions. The Debian Mentors community "
"<https://wiki.debian.org/DebianMentors> is happy to help if you have "
"questions."
msgstr ""
"Använd B<bts> och BTS i allmänhet ansvarsfullt. Börja med att prenumerera på"
" paket, pts-subscribe(1), eller särskilda felrapporter som intresserar dig, "
"”bts subscribe 69042”. Försök följa andra Debianbidragsgivares arbetssätt. "
"Gemenskapen Debian Mentors <https://wiki.debian.org/DebianMentors> hjälper "
"gärna om du har frågor."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:421
msgid ""
"You can find more on how we work at <https://wiki.debian.org/BugTriage> and "
"<https://wiki.debian.org/BugReport/WorkingOn>."
msgstr ""
"Du kan läsa mer om hur vi arbetar på <https://wiki.debian.org/BugTriage> och"
" <https://wiki.debian.org/BugReport/WorkingOn>."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:424
msgid ""
"Mistakes happen, but consider that other busy volunteers may have to use "
"time they could otherwise spend fixing bugs to help you clean them up."
msgstr ""
"Misstag händer, men tänk på att andra upptagna volontärer kan behöva lägga "
"tid som de annars kunde ha använt till att rätta felrapporter på att hjälpa "
"dig städa upp efter dem."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:427
msgid ""
"To learn from other people in an in-person setting you may find a Bug "
"Squashing Party or more general Debian Event to attend near you: "
"<https://wiki.debian.org/BSP>, <https://wiki.debian.org/DebianEvents>."
msgstr ""
"För att lära av andra personligen kan du hitta ett Bug Squashing Party eller"
" ett annat Debianevenemang nära dig: <https://wiki.debian.org/BSP>, "
"<https://wiki.debian.org/DebianEvents>."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:433
msgid "Workflows"
msgstr "Arbetsflöden"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:435
msgid ""
"B<bts> supports reading bugs in a web- or e-mail-based worflow, but to make "
"changes B<bts> will always send e-mail to a BTS I<service> e-mail address "
"(I<service>B<@bugs.debian.org>)."
msgstr ""
"B<bts> stöder läsning av felrapporter på webben och via epost, men för att "
"göra ändringar skickar B<bts> alltid epost till en BTS tjänsteadress, "
"I<service>B<@bugs.debian.org>."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:439
msgid ""
"The web-based workflow supports both graphical and command-line browsers. "
"While graphical browsers such as firefox or chromium may be familiar, you "
"should consider traditional command-line browsers such as w3m(1) or lynx(1) "
"for allowing a more focused workflow without context switches out of your "
"terminal."
msgstr ""
"Det webbaserade arbetsflödet stöder både grafiska webbläsare och "
"kommandoradswebbläsare. Även om grafiska webbläsare som Firefox eller "
"Chromium kanske är bekanta, bör du överväga traditionella "
"kommandoradswebbläsare som w3m(1) eller lynx(1) för att möjliggöra ett mer "
"fokuserat arbetsflöde utan kontextbyten utanför din terminal."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:445
msgid ""
"The software running the Debian BTS, \"Debbugs\", has first-class support "
"for these browsers being from the same era of computing."
msgstr ""
"Programvaran som driver Debians BTS, ”Debbugs”, har förstklassigt stöd för "
"dessa webbläsare eftersom de kommer från samma datorera."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:448
msgid ""
"To make reading and changing bugs enjoyable a highly configurable command-"
"line e-mail client (MUA) such as mutt(1), neomutt(1) or aerc(1) is "
"recommended. By using B<bts reply> and B<bts context> together with your "
"MUA's pipe command you can make full use of B<bts> without so much as "
"leaving your MUA. WARNING: Terminal mailing can be *highly* addictive."
msgstr ""
"För att göra det trevligt att läsa och ändra felrapporter rekommenderas en "
"mycket konfigurerbar e-postklient för kommandoraden (MUA), som mutt(1), "
"neomutt(1) eller aerc(1). Genom att använda B<bts reply> och B<bts context> "
"tillsammans med MUA:ns rörledningskommando kan du använda B<bts> fullt ut "
"utan att lämna MUA:n. VARNING: Terminalbaserad e-post kan vara *mycket* "
"beroendeframkallande."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:455
msgid "E-Mail Processing"
msgstr "E-postbehandling"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:457
msgid ""
"Being E-Mail BTS change requests are asynchrounous and may take considerable"
" time to get through anti-spam measures. You should expect up to half an "
"hour of delay when making your first change."
msgstr ""
"Ändringsbegäranden till BTS via epost är asynkrona och kan ta avsevärd tid "
"att passera skräppostskyddet. Räkna med upp till en halvtimmes fördröjning "
"när du gör din första ändring."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:461
msgid ""
"You will receive an acknowledgment mail from the BTS when the changes are "
"accepted. You can file ACK messages into a folder for mail delivery "
"troubleshooting purposes (check the B<X-Debian-PR-Message:> header for "
"automated filtering) or suppress them using B<--no-ack> or "
"B<BTS_SUPPRESS_ACKS>=yes."
msgstr ""
"Du får ett bekräftelsemeddelande från BTS när ändringarna godtas. Du kan "
"arkivera ACK meddelanden i en mapp för felsökning av epostleverans, "
"kontrollera huvudfältet B<X-Debian-PR-Message:> för automatisk filtrering, "
"eller undertrycka dem med B<--no-ack> eller B<BTS_SUPPRESS_ACKS>=yes."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:467
msgid "Sending E-Mail"
msgstr "Skicka e-post"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:469
msgid ""
"To get started with B<bts> right now use B<--smtp-reportbug> to send emails "
"exclusively to BTS addresses without having to worry about configuration "
"until you need more."
msgstr ""
"Använd B<--smtp-reportbug> för att komma igång med B<bts> och skicka e-post "
"enbart till BTS-adresser utan att behöva bekymra dig om konfiguration förrän"
" du behöver mer."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:473
msgid ""
"Once you want to send mail directly to wider internet destinations outside "
"BTS mail addresses (for CC'ing people) B<bts> supports the following:"
msgstr ""
"När du vill skicka e-post direkt till fler internetadresser utanför BTS-e-"
"postadresserna (för att CC:a personer) stöder B<bts> följande:"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:478
msgid ""
"* interactive command-line E-Mail clients (MUAs): B<mutt>, B<neomutt> and "
"B<aerc> using B<--mutt>,"
msgstr ""
"* interaktiva e-postklienter för kommandoraden (MUA:er): B<mutt>, B<neomutt>"
" och B<aerc> med B<--mutt>,"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:480
msgid "* connecting directly to an SMTP server using B<--smtp-host>,"
msgstr "* anslutning direkt till en SMTP-server med B<--smtp-host>,"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:482
msgid "* system mailer (B<sendmail> compatible) (see B<--sendmail>)"
msgstr ""
"* systemets epostprogram, kompatibelt med B<sendmail>, se B<--sendmail>"

#. type: =for
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:484
msgid ""
"comment TIL history: mail is oldest, then came sendmail, then mailx.  See "
"https://heirloom.sourceforge.net/mailx_history.html"
msgstr ""
"kommentar om TIL-historik: mail är äldst, sedan kom sendmail och därefter "
"mailx.  Se https://heirloom.sourceforge.net/mailx_history.html"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:489
msgid "Control Commands"
msgstr "Kontrollkommandon"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:491
msgid ""
"The commands used by B<bts> mirror Debbugs control commands but with support"
" for abbreviations, more relaxed syntax and helpful local validation and "
"cross-checking of the current bug state on the BTS server."
msgstr ""
"Kommandona som används av B<bts> motsvarar Debbugs kontrollkommandon, men "
"stöder förkortningar, friare syntax samt användbar lokal validering och "
"kontroll av aktuell felstatus på BTS-servern."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:495
msgid ""
"Debbugs control reference: <https://www.debian.org/Bugs/server-control>"
msgstr ""
"Referens för Debbugs-kontroll: <https://www.debian.org/Bugs/server-control>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:497
msgid ""
"B<bts> is also less strict about what constitutes a valid bug number. For "
"example the following are understood:"
msgstr ""
"B<bts> är också mindre strikt med vad som utgör ett giltigt felnummer. Till "
"exempel förstås följande:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:500
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts severity Bug#85942 normal\n"
" $ bts severity \\#85942 normal\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts severity Bug#85942 normal\n"
" $ bts severity \\#85942 normal\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:503
msgid ""
"In the latter command a POSIX shell will interpret the hash (\"#\") as "
"starting a a comment since it's not in the middle of a shellword, so you "
"need to quote or escape it it as we've done here."
msgstr ""
"I det senare kommandot tolkar ett POSIX skal hashtecknet, ”#”, som början på"
" en kommentar eftersom det inte står mitt i ett skalord. Du måste därför "
"citera det eller föregå det med ett omvänt snedstreck, som här."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:507
msgid ""
"B<bts> allows you to abbreviate commands to the shortest unique substring. "
"It understands \"bts cl 85942\" as an alias for the \"close\" command."
msgstr ""
"B<bts> låter dig förkorta kommandon till den kortaste unika delsträngen. Det"
" tolkar ”bts cl 85942” som alias för kommandot ”close”."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:512
msgid "Control Command Comments"
msgstr "Kommentarer till kontrollkommandon"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:514
msgid ""
"It is possible to add comments to BTS control commands to explain why the "
"changes were made:"
msgstr ""
"Du kan lägga till kommentarer till BTS-kontrollkommandon för att förklara "
"varför ändringarna gjordes:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:517
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts severity 30321 normal \\#Not as severe as claimed\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts severity 30321 normal \\#Inte så allvarligt som påstås\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:519
msgid ""
"Note that POSIX shells will remove these comments unless the hash \"#\" "
"comment character is escaped with a backslash as we've done above or quoted "
"with single '' or double quotes \"\" as below."
msgstr ""
"Observera att POSIX-skal tar bort dessa kommentarer om hashtecknet ”#” inte "
"skyddas med ett omvänt snedstreck, som ovan, eller citeras med enkla '' "
"eller dubbla citattecken ””, som nedan."

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:523
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts severity 30321 normal '# Still not all that severe'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts severity 30321 normal '# Fortfarande inte så allvarligt'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:525
msgid ""
"Generally speaking it's preferred to use the B<reply> command to include "
"C<Control> pseudoheaders in your response to the bug report instead. However"
" including comments can still be useful in that context to document what you"
" want to achieve to other contributors in complex cases."
msgstr ""
"I allmänhet är det bättre att använda kommandot B<reply> för att lägga till "
"C<Control>-pseudohuvuden i svaret på felrapporten. Kommentarer kan dock "
"fortfarande vara användbara för att dokumentera vad du vill uppnå för andra "
"bidragsgivare i komplexa fall."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:531
msgid "Multiple Commands"
msgstr "Flera kommandon"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:533
msgid ""
"You can send multiple commands in a single e-mail by separating them with a "
"period or comma, like so:"
msgstr ""
"Du kan skicka flera kommandon i samma e-postmeddelande genom att skilja dem "
"med punkt eller komma, så här:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:536
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts severity 95672 normal , done 96642 0.38-7 \\#Fixed by fix-it.patch\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts severity 95672 normal , done 96642 0.38-7 \\#Fixat med fix-it.patch\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:538
msgid ""
"It is important the commas are surrounded by whitespace so your shell passes"
" them to B<bts> as distinct arguments."
msgstr ""
"Det är viktigt att kommatecknen omges av blanksteg så att skalet skickar dem"
" till B<bts> som separata argument."

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:541
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts severity 95672 normal , merge 95672 95673 \\#they are the same!\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts severity 95672 normal , merge 95672 95673 \\#de är identiska!\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:544
msgid "Consistency Checks"
msgstr "Konsistenskontroller"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:546
msgid ""
"Many commands support internal and online consistency checks. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Många kommandon stöder interna och onlinebaserade konsistenskontroller. Till"
" exempel:"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:550
msgid ""
"* B<fixed>, B<found>: complain when the record that's being made already "
"exists in the BTS,"
msgstr "* B<fixed>, B<found>: varna när posten som skapas redan finns i BTS,"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:553
msgid ""
"* B<notfixed>, B<notfound>: complain when the record being removed doesn't "
"exist,"
msgstr "* B<notfixed>, B<notfound>: varna när posten som tas bort inte finns,"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:555
msgid "* B<done>: checks whether the bug is alread marked 'done',"
msgstr "* B<done>: kontrollerar om felrapporten redan är markerad som 'done',"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:557
msgid ""
"* B<archive>, B<unarchive>: check whether the bug is already/not yet "
"archived."
msgstr ""
"* B<archive>, B<unarchive>: kontrollerar om felrapporten redan/inte ännu är "
"arkiverad."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:561
msgid ""
"When multiple commands all checks must succeed before any email is sent so "
"you may fearlessly iterate on B<bts> commands."
msgstr ""
"När flera kommandon används måste alla kontroller lyckas innan e-post "
"skickas, så att du tryggt kan iterera med B<bts>-kommandon."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:564
msgid ""
"Many of the checks involve fetching online information from the BTS. Use "
"B<--offline> to disable these. Purely B<bts> internal consistency checks "
"such as marking the same bug as B<done> twice cannot be bypassed this way."
msgstr ""
"Många kontroller hämtar onlineinformation från BTS. Använd B<--offline> för "
"att inaktivera dem. Rent interna konsistenskontroller i B<bts>, som att "
"markera samma felrapport som B<done> två gånger, kan inte kringgås på detta "
"sätt."

#. type: =head2
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:569
msgid "The Implicit Bug"
msgstr "Den underförstådda felrapporten"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:571
msgid ""
"To refer to the last mentioned bug number minus one \"-1\" may be used. The "
"deprecated alias \"it\" is also allowed. For example you could write:"
msgstr ""
"För att hänvisa till senast nämnda felnummer kan minus ett, ”-1”, användas. "
"Det föråldrade aliaset ”it” är också tillåtet. Du kan till exempel skriva:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:574
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts severity 95672 wishlist , retitle -1 bts: please add a foo option\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts severity 95672 wishlist , retitle -1 bts: lägg till ett foo-alternativ\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:576
msgid ""
"Alternatively you can also omit the bug number entirely as long as the "
"resulting usage is unambigous, i.e. the argument(s) don't look like bug-"
"numbers."
msgstr ""
"Alternativt kan du helt utelämna felnumret så länge den resulterande "
"användningen är entydig, det vill säga att argumenten inte ser ut som "
"felnummer."

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:580
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts done 95672 , fixed 0.1-3\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts done 95672 , fixed 0.1-3\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:582
msgid ""
"Every command allows at least one keyword of "
"B<to>/B<by>/B<from>/B<with>/B<since>/B<email>/B<+>/B<->/B<=> (see "
"B<COMMANDS>) to disambiguate the meaning."
msgstr ""
"Varje kommando tillåter minst ett nyckelord av "
"B<to>/B<by>/B<from>/B<with>/B<since>/B<email>/B<+>/B<->/B<=> (se "
"B<COMMANDS>) för att undanröja tvetydighet."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:586
msgid ""
"Commands that take multiple bug numbers (B<assign>/B<merge>/B<blocked>)  "
"require the use of a keyword to omit the implicit bug argument, but it is "
"optional for other commands."
msgstr ""
"Kommandon som tar flera felnummer (B<assign>/B<merge>/B<blocked>) kräver ett"
" nyckelord för att utelämna argumentet för den underförstådda felrapporten, "
"men det är valfritt för andra kommandon."

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:590
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts reopen 95672 , merge with 123456   # is equivalent to:\n"
" $ bts reopen 95672 , merge -1 123456\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts reopen 95672 , merge with 123456 # motsvarar:\n"
" $ bts reopen 95672 , merge -1 123456\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:593
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts reopen 95672 , blocked by 123456   # is equivalent to:\n"
" $ bts reopen 95672 , blocked -1 123456\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts reopen 95672 , blocked by 123456   # motsvarar:\n"
" $ bts reopen 95672 , blocked -1 123456\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:596
msgid ""
"When the B<clone> command is involved the meaning of -1 can become "
"confusing. Below we allocate -1 as a \"new ID\" instead of using it to refer"
" to the previously mentioned bug number 95672. Consequently:"
msgstr ""
"När kommandot B<clone> används kan betydelsen av -1 bli förvirrande. Nedan "
"tilldelar vi -1 som ett ”nytt ID” i stället för att använda det för att "
"hänvisa till tidigare nämnda felnummer 95672. Följaktligen:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:600
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts done 95672 , clone to -1 -2        # is equivalent to:\n"
" $ bts done 95672 , clone 95672 to -1 -2\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts done 95672 , clone to -1 -2 # motsvarar:\n"
" $ bts done 95672 , clone 95672 to -1 -2\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:603
msgid "and similarly"
msgstr "och på samma sätt"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:605
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts done 95672 , clone -1 -1 -2        # expands to:\n"
" $ bts done 95672 , clone 95672 -1 -2\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts done 95672 , clone -1 -1 -2 # expanderas till:\n"
" $ bts done 95672 , clone 95672 -1 -2\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:608
msgid ""
"Further, after the B<clone -1> command 'B<-1>' no longer refers to the "
"implicit bug number, but rather the number newly allocated by the BTS "
"server. You can use 'B<it>' or the keyword syntax to disambiguate."
msgstr ""
"Efter kommandot B<clone -1> hänvisar ”B<-1>” inte längre till det "
"underförstådda felnumret, utan till numret som BTS-servern just tilldelade. "
"Du kan använda ”B<it>” eller nyckelordssyntax för att undanröja tvetydighet."

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:612
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts clone 95672 to -1 -2 , done        # expands to:\n"
" $ bts clone 95672 to -1 -2 , done 95672\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts clone 95672 to -1 -2 , done        # expanderas till:\n"
" $ bts clone 95672 to -1 -2 , done 95672\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:615
msgid "whereas"
msgstr "medan"

#. type: verbatim
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:617
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ bts clone 95672 to -1 -2 , done -1     # is already fully expanded.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ bts clone 95672 to -1 -2 , done -1     # är redan helt expanderat.\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:622
msgid ""
"B<bts> examines the B<devscripts> configuration files as described below.  "
"Command-line options override the configuration file settings as you'd "
"expect."
msgstr ""
"B<bts> läser konfigurationsfilerna för B<devscripts> enligt beskrivningen "
"nedan. Kommandoradsalternativ åsidosätter inställningarna i "
"konfigurationsfilen som väntat."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:628
msgid "Workflow Mode Options"
msgstr "Alternativ för arbetsflödesläge"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:630
msgid "See also \"Workflows\" in B<DESCRIPTION>."
msgstr "Se även \"Arbetsflöden\" i B<DESCRIPTION>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:634
msgid "B<-o>, B<--offline>"
msgstr "B<-o>, B<--offline>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:636
msgid ""
"Make B<bts> use cached bugs for the B<show> and B<bugs> commands, if a cache"
" is available for the requested data. See the B<cache> command, below for "
"information on setting up a cache."
msgstr ""
"Låt B<bts> använda cachade felrapporter för kommandona B<show> och B<bugs> "
"om det finns en cache för begärd information. Se kommandot B<cache> nedan "
"för information om hur en cache ställs in."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:640
msgid "B<--online>, B<--no-offline>"
msgstr "B<--online>, B<--no-offline>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:642
msgid ""
"Opposite of B<--offline>; overrides any configuration file directive to work"
" offline."
msgstr ""
"Motsatsen till B<--offline>; åsidosätter alla konfigurationsfildirektiv för "
"offlinearbete."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:645
msgid "B<-m>|B<--mail>|B<--mbox>"
msgstr "B<-m>|B<--mail>|B<--mbox>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:647
msgid ""
"Use command-line e-mail workflow for reading bugs and sending change request"
" emails. When asked to display bugs invoke a mail reader (B<--mailreader>, "
"B<BTS_MAIL_READER>). When sending emails default to composing in a command-"
"line email client (B<--mutt>, B<BTS_MUTT_COMMAND>)."
msgstr ""
"Använd e-postarbetsflöde på kommandoraden för att läsa felrapporter och "
"skicka e-post med ändringsbegäranden. När felrapporter ska visas startas en "
"e-postläsare (B<--mailreader>, B<BTS_MAIL_READER>). När e-post skickas "
"används som standard en e-postklient för kommandoraden (B<--mutt>, "
"B<BTS_MUTT_COMMAND>)."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:652
msgid "B<-w>|B<--web>"
msgstr "B<-w>|B<--web>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:654
msgid ""
"Use web workflow for reading bugs. Opposite of B<--mail>. When asked to "
"display bugs use a web-browser (I<$BROWSER> or sensible-browser(1))."
msgstr ""
"Använd webbarbetsflöde för att läsa felrapporter. Motsatsen till B<--mail>. "
"När felrapporter ska visas används en webbläsare (I<$BROWSER> eller "
"sensible-browser(1))."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:659
msgid "B<-n>, B<--no-action>"
msgstr "B<-n>, B<--no-action>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:661
msgid "Do not send emails but print them to standard output."
msgstr "Skicka inte e-post utan skriv ut den till standardutmatningen."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:663
msgid "B<--cache>, B<--no-cache>"
msgstr "B<--cache>, B<--no-cache>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:665
msgid ""
"Should we attempt to cache new versions of BTS pages when performing "
"B<show>/B<bugs> commands? Default is to cache."
msgstr ""
"Ska vi försöka cachelagra nya versioner av BTS-sidor när kommandona "
"B<show>/B<bugs> körs? Standard är cachelagring."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:668
msgid "B<--cache-mode=>{B<min>|B<mbox>|B<full>}"
msgstr "B<--cache-mode=>{B<min>|B<mbox>|B<full>}"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:670
msgid ""
"When running a B<bts cache> command, should we only mirror the basic bug "
"(B<min>), or should we also mirror the mbox version (B<mbox>), or should we "
"mirror the whole thing, including the mbox and the boring attachments to the"
" BTS bug pages and the acknowledgement emails (B<full>)? Default is B<min>."
msgstr ""
"När kommandot B<bts cache> körs, ska endast den grundläggande felrapporten "
"(B<min>) speglas, även mbox-versionen (B<mbox>) eller allt, inklusive mbox, "
"bilagorna till BTS-felrapportsidorna och bekräftelsemeddelandena (B<full>)? "
"Standard är B<min>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:676
msgid "B<--cache-delay=>I<seconds>"
msgstr "B<--cache-delay=>I<seconds>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:678
msgid ""
"Time in seconds to delay between each download, to avoid hammering the BTS "
"web server. Default is 0 seconds."
msgstr ""
"Fördröjning i sekunder mellan varje nedladdning för att undvika att "
"överbelasta BTS-webbservern. Standard är 0 sekunder."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:681
msgid "B<--mailreader=>I<COMMAND>"
msgstr "B<--mailreader=>I<COMMAND>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:683
msgid "A (shell) command invoked to read a bug mailbox."
msgstr "Ett skal-kommando som anropas för att läsa en felrapportsbrevlåda."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:685
msgid ""
"The I<COMMAND> must contain the replacement marker \"B<%s>\" which is "
"expanded to path to an mbox file."
msgstr ""
"I<COMMAND> måste innehålla ersättningsmarkören ”B<%s>”, som expanderas till "
"sökvägen till en mbox-fil."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:688
msgid ""
"Default depends on mailreaders available on the system. See "
"B<BTS_MAIL_READER> config option."
msgstr ""
"Standardvärdet beror på vilka e-postläsare som finns tillgängliga i "
"systemet. Se konfigurationsalternativet B<BTS_MAIL_READER>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:691
msgid "B<--cc-addr=>I<CC_EMAIL_ADDRESS>"
msgstr "B<--cc-addr=>I<CC_EMAIL_ADDRESS>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:693
msgid ""
"Send carbon copies to a list of users. I<CC_EMAIL_ADDRESS> should be a "
"comma-separated list of email addresses. Multiple options add more CCs."
msgstr ""
"Skicka kopior till en lista med användare. I<CC_EMAIL_ADDRESS> ska vara en "
"kommaseparerad lista med e-postadresser. Flera alternativ lägger till fler "
"CC-kopior."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:696
msgid "B<--use-default-cc>"
msgstr "B<--use-default-cc>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:698
msgid ""
"Add the addresses specified in the configuration file option "
"B<BTS_DEFAULT_CC> to the list specified using B<--cc-addr>.  This is the "
"default."
msgstr ""
"Lägg till adresserna som anges i konfigurationsfilalternativet "
"B<BTS_DEFAULT_CC> till listan som anges med B<--cc-addr>. Detta är standard."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:702
msgid "B<--no-use-default-cc>"
msgstr "B<--no-use-default-cc>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:704
msgid ""
"Do not add addresses specified in B<BTS_DEFAULT_CC> to the carbon copy list."
msgstr ""
"Lägg inte till adresser som anges i B<BTS_DEFAULT_CC> till listan över "
"kopior."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:707 ../scripts/mass-bug.pl:116
msgid "B<--sendmail=>I<SENDMAILCMD>"
msgstr "B<--sendmail=>I<SENDMAILCMD>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:709
msgid ""
"Specify the system mailer (B<sendmail> compatible) command to use for "
"sending email."
msgstr ""
"Ange systemets e-postprogramkommando (B<sendmail>-kompatibelt) för att "
"skicka e-post."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:712
msgid ""
"The command will be split on white space and will not be passed to a shell."
"  Default is F</usr/sbin/sendmail>.  The B<-t> option will be automatically "
"added if the command is F</usr/sbin/sendmail> or F</usr/sbin/exim*>.  For "
"other mailers, if they require a B<-t> option, this must be included in the "
"I<SENDMAILCMD>, for example: B<--sendmail=\"/usr/sbin/mymailer -t\">."
msgstr ""
"Kommandot delas upp efter blanksteg och skickas inte vidare till ett skal.  "
"Standardinställningen är F</usr/sbin/sendmail>.  Alternativet B<-t> läggs "
"automatiskt till om kommandot är F</usr/sbin/sendmail> eller "
"F</usr/sbin/exim*>.  För andra e-postprogram som kräver alternativet B<-t> "
"måste detta inkluderas i I<SENDMAILCMD>, till exempel: "
"B<--sendmail=\"/usr/sbin/mymailer -t\">."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:718
msgid ""
"Conflicts with explicit B<--mutt>, B<--smtp-hots> and B<--smtp-reportbug>. "
"Overrides implicit B<--mutt> and B<BTS_SMTP_HOST>."
msgstr ""
"Konflikter med uttryckliga B<--mutt>, B<--smtp-hots> och B<--smtp-"
"reportbug>. Åsidosätter underförstådda B<--mutt> och B<BTS_SMTP_HOST>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:721 ../scripts/nmudiff.1:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--mutt>"
msgstr "B<--mutt>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:723
msgid ""
"Use interactive command line mail client (B<BTS_MUTT_COMMAND>) for sending "
"of mails instead of SMTP (B<--smtp-host>) or system mailer (B<--sendmail>)."
msgstr ""
"Använd en interaktiv e-postklient för kommandoraden (B<BTS_MUTT_COMMAND>) "
"för att skicka e-post i stället för SMTP (B<--smtp-host>) eller systemets "
"e-postprogram (B<--sendmail>)."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:726
msgid ""
"Note that one of B<$DEBEMAIL> or B<$EMAIL> must be set in the environment in"
" order to use B<mutt> to send emails."
msgstr ""
"Observera att en av B<$DEBEMAIL> eller B<$EMAIL> måste anges i miljön för "
"att B<mutt> ska kunna användas för att skicka e-post."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:729
msgid ""
"If B<--mutt> is given B<--interactive> and B<--force-interactive> are "
"ineffective."
msgstr ""
"Om B<--mutt> anges är B<--interactive> och B<--force-interactive> "
"ineffektiva."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:732
msgid ""
"B<--mutt> is implied when B<bts> is invoked from inside a command-line mail "
"client as determined by $_ (see B<BTS_MUTT_COMMAND> for detailed logic) and "
"e-mail workflow is active (B<--mail>, B<BTS_WORKFLOW=mail>)."
msgstr ""
"B<--mutt> används underförstått när B<bts> anropas från en e-postklient för "
"kommandoraden, enligt vad $_ anger (se B<BTS_MUTT_COMMAND> för detaljerad "
"logik), och e-postarbetsflödet är aktivt (B<--mail>, B<BTS_WORKFLOW=mail>)."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:736 ../scripts/nmudiff.1:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--no-mutt>"
msgstr "B<--no-mutt>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:738
msgid ""
"Cancel implicit or explicit B<--mutt> reverting to sending with SMTP or "
"system mailer instead."
msgstr ""
"Avbryt underförstådda eller uttryckliga B<--mutt> och återgå till att skicka"
" via SMTP eller systemets e-postprogram."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:741
msgid "B<--soap-timeout=>I<SECONDS>"
msgstr "B<--soap-timeout=>I<SECONDS>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:743
msgid ""
"Timeout when fetching bug status information from the BTS in B<--online> "
"mode."
msgstr ""
"Tidsgräns vid hämtning av felstatusinformation från BTS i B<--online>-läge."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:746
msgid ""
"Defaults to 5 seconds when B<--interactive> or B<--mutt> are active; 30 "
"seconds otherwise (B<--no-interactive>)."
msgstr ""
"Standardvärdet är 5 sekunder när B<--interactive> eller B<--mutt> är aktiva;"
" annars 30 sekunder (B<--no-interactive>)."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:749
msgid "B<--smtp-host=>I<SMTPHOST>"
msgstr "B<--smtp-host=>I<SMTPHOST>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:751
msgid ""
"Specify an SMTP host.  If given, B<bts> will send mail by talking directly "
"to this SMTP host rather than by invoking a B<sendmail> command."
msgstr ""
"Ange en SMTP-värd. Om den anges skickar B<bts> e-post genom att kommunicera "
"direkt med denna SMTP-värd i stället för att anropa ett "
"B<sendmail>-kommando."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:754
msgid ""
"The host name may be followed by a colon (\":\") and a port number in order "
"to use a port other than the default.  It may also begin with \"ssmtp://\" "
"or \"smtps://\" to indicate that SMTPS should be used."
msgstr ""
"Värdnamnet kan följas av ett kolon (\":\") och ett portnummer för att "
"använda en annan port än standardporten. Det kan också börja med "
"\"ssmtp://\" eller \"smtps://\" för att ange att SMTPS ska användas."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:758
msgid ""
"If SMTPS not specified, B<bts> will still try to use STARTTLS if it's "
"advertised by the SMTP host."
msgstr ""
"Om SMTPS inte anges försöker B<bts> ändå använda STARTTLS om SMTP-värden "
"annonserar det."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:761
msgid ""
"Note that one of B<$DEBEMAIL> or B<$EMAIL> must be set in the environment in"
" order to use direct SMTP connections to send emails."
msgstr ""
"Observera att antingen B<$DEBEMAIL> eller B<$EMAIL> måste vara satt i miljön"
" för att använda direkta SMTP-anslutningar för att skicka e-post."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:764
msgid ""
"Conflicts with B<--mutt> and B<--sendmail>. Overridden by B<--smtp-"
"reportbug>."
msgstr ""
"Konflikter med B<--mutt> och B<--sendmail>. Åsidosätts av B<--smtp-"
"reportbug>."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:766
msgid "B<--smtp-reportbug>"
msgstr "B<--smtp-reportbug>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:768
msgid ""
"Use the the reportbug.debian.org SMTP server to send bug reports and change "
"requests (no account registration or authentication needed)."
msgstr ""
"Använd SMTP-servern reportbug.debian.org för att skicka felrapporter och "
"ändringsbegäranden (ingen kontoregistrering eller autentisering krävs)."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:771
msgid "Equivalent to B<--smtp-host=reportbug.debian.org:587 --interactive>."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<--smtp-host=reportbug.debian.org:587 --interactive>."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:773
msgid ""
"Note that reportbug.debian.org is rate limited to a small number of mails "
"per hour and only email destined for bugs.debian.org is accepted. "
"Consequently using B<--cc-addr>, B<BTS_DEFAULT_CC>, B<reply> or B<reassign> "
"commands will likeley cause mails to be rejected while sending."
msgstr ""
"Observera att reportbug.debian.org är begränsad till ett litet antal "
"e-postmeddelanden per timme och bara accepterar e-post till bugs.debian.org."
" Därför leder användning av B<--cc-addr>, B<BTS_DEFAULT_CC>, B<reply> eller "
"B<reassign> sannolikt till att e-post avvisas vid sändning."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:779
msgid "B<--smtp-username=>I<USERNAME>, B<--smtp-password=>I<PASSWORD>"
msgstr "B<--smtp-username=>I<USERNAME>, B<--smtp-password=>I<PASSWORD>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:781
msgid ""
"Specify the credentials to use when connecting to the SMTP server specified "
"by B<--smtp-host>.  If the server does not require authentication then these"
" options should not be used."
msgstr ""
"Ange autentiseringsuppgifterna som ska användas vid anslutning till SMTP-"
"servern som anges med B<--smtp-host>. Om servern inte kräver autentisering "
"ska dessa alternativ inte användas."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:785
msgid ""
"If a username is specified but not a password, B<bts> will prompt for the "
"password before sending the mail."
msgstr ""
"Om ett användarnamn anges men inget lösenord frågar B<bts> efter lösenordet "
"innan e-post skickas."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:788
msgid "B<--smtp-helo=>I<HELO>"
msgstr "B<--smtp-helo=>I<HELO>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:790
msgid ""
"Specify the name to use in the I<HELO> command when connecting to the SMTP "
"server; defaults to the contents of the file F</etc/mailname>, if it exists."
msgstr ""
"Ange namnet som ska användas i kommandot I<HELO> vid anslutning till SMTP-"
"servern; standard är innehållet i filen F</etc/mailname>, om den finns."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:794
msgid ""
"Note that some SMTP servers may reject the use of a I<HELO> which either "
"does not resolve or does not appear to belong to the host using it."
msgstr ""
"Observera att vissa SMTP-servrar kan avvisa ett I<HELO> som antingen inte "
"kan lösas upp eller inte verkar tillhöra värden som använder det."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:797
msgid "B<--bts-server>"
msgstr "B<--bts-server>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:799
msgid "Use a debbugs server other than the default https://bugs.debian.org."
msgstr ""
"Använd en annan Debbugs-server än standardservern https://bugs.debian.org."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:801
msgid "B<-f>, B<--force-refresh>"
msgstr "B<-f>, B<--force-refresh>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:803
msgid ""
"Download a bug report again, even if it does not appear to have changed "
"since the last B<cache> command.  Useful if a B<--cache-mode=full> is "
"requested for the first time (otherwise unchanged bug reports will not be "
"downloaded again, even if the boring bits have not been downloaded)."
msgstr ""
"Hämta en felrapport igen även om den inte verkar ha ändrats sedan senaste "
"B<cache>-kommandot. Användbart om B<--cache-mode=full> begärs för första "
"gången (annars hämtas inte oförändrade felrapporter igen, även om de mindre "
"intressanta delarna inte har hämtats)."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:809
msgid "B<--no-force-refresh>"
msgstr "B<--no-force-refresh>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:811
msgid "Suppress any configuration file B<--force-refresh> option."
msgstr ""
"Undertryck ett eventuellt B<--force-refresh>-alternativ i "
"konfigurationsfilen."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:813
msgid "B<--only-new>"
msgstr "B<--only-new>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:815
msgid ""
"Download only new bugs when caching. Do not check for updates in bugs we "
"already have."
msgstr ""
"Hämta endast nya felrapporter vid cachelagring. Kontrollera inte "
"uppdateringar av felrapporter som redan finns."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:818
msgid "B<--include-resolved>"
msgstr "B<--include-resolved>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:820
msgid ""
"When caching bug reports, include those that are marked as resolved.  This "
"is the default behaviour."
msgstr ""
"Inkludera felrapporter som är markerade som lösta vid cachelagring. Detta är"
" standardbeteendet."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:823
msgid "B<--no-include-resolved>"
msgstr "B<--no-include-resolved>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:825
msgid ""
"Reverse the behaviour of the previous option.  That is, do not cache bugs "
"that are marked as resolved."
msgstr ""
"Vänd beteendet för föregående alternativ. Cachelagra alltså inte "
"felrapporter som är markerade som lösta."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:828
msgid "B<--no-ack>"
msgstr "B<--no-ack>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:830
msgid ""
"Suppress acknowledgment mails from the BTS.  Note that this will only affect"
" the copies of messages CCed to bugs, not those sent to the control bot."
msgstr ""
"Undertryck bekräftelsemeddelanden från BTS. Detta påverkar endast kopior av "
"meddelanden som CC:ats till felrapporter, inte dem som skickas till "
"kontrollboten."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:834
msgid "B<--ack>"
msgstr "B<--ack>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:836
msgid "Do not suppress acknowledgement mails.  This is the default behaviour."
msgstr "Undertryck inte bekräftelsemeddelanden.  Detta är standardbeteendet."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:838 ../scripts/tagpending.pl:136
msgid "B<-i>, B<--interactive>"
msgstr "B<-i>, B<--interactive>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:840
msgid ""
"Before sending an e-mail, display the content and allow it to be edited, or "
"the sending cancelled."
msgstr ""
"Före sändning av e-post, visa innehållet och tillåt redigering eller att "
"sändningen avbryts."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:843
msgid "B<--force-interactive>"
msgstr "B<--force-interactive>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:845
msgid ""
"Force interactive editing immediately. Similar to B<--interactive>, except "
"editor is spawned before the send/cancel/edit prompt."
msgstr ""
"Tvinga fram interaktiv redigering omedelbart. Liknar B<--interactive>, men "
"redigeraren startas före frågan om att skicka, avbryta eller redigera."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:848
msgid "B<--no-interactive>"
msgstr "B<--no-interactive>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:850
msgid "Immediately send bug change request e-mails without confirmation."
msgstr "Skicka e-post med feländringsbegäran omedelbart utan bekräftelse."

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:852
msgid ""
"This is the default behaviour except if B<--mutt> is implicitly active and "
"for some commands which require composing a written reply (B<done>, "
"B<reply>)."
msgstr ""
"Detta är standardbeteendet, utom om B<--mutt> är underförstått aktivt och "
"för kommandon som kräver att ett skriftligt svar formuleras (B<done>, "
"B<reply>)."

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:855 ../scripts/build-rdeps.pl:116 ../scripts/dget.pl:646
msgid "B<-q>, B<--quiet>"
msgstr "B<-q>, B<--quiet>"

#. type: textblock
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:857
msgid ""
"When running B<bts cache>, only display information about newly cached "
"pages, not messages saying already cached.  If this option is specified "
"twice, only output error messages (to stderr)."
msgstr ""
"När B<bts cache> körs, visa bara information om nyligen cachelagrade sidor "
"och inte meddelanden om sidor som redan finns i cachen. Om alternativet "
"anges två gånger visas bara felmeddelanden (till stderr)."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/bts.pl:861 ../scripts/debc.1:95 ../scripts/debchange.1:390
#: ../scripts/debclean.1:80 ../scripts/debdiff.1:177 ../scripts/debi.1:101
