#. type: TH
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEBUILD"
msgstr "DEBUILD"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:4
msgid "debuild - build a Debian package"
msgstr "debuild – bygg ett Debian-paket"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:7
msgid ""
"B<debuild> [I<debuild options>] [I<dpkg-buildpackage options>] [B<--lintian-"
"opts> I<lintian options>]"
msgstr ""
"B<debuild> [I<debuild options>] [I<dpkg-buildpackage options>] [B<--lintian-"
"opts> I<lintian options>]"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:10
msgid ""
"B<debuild> [I<debuild options>] -- B<binary>|B<binary-arch>|B<binary-"
"indep>|B<clean> ..."
msgstr ""
"B<debuild> [I<debuild options>] -- B<binary>|B<binary-arch>|B<binary-"
"indep>|B<clean> ..."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:31
msgid ""
"B<debuild> creates all the files necessary for uploading a Debian package.  "
"It first runs B<dpkg-buildpackage>, then runs B<lintian> on the I<.changes> "
"file created (assuming that B<lintian> is installed), and finally signs the "
"appropriate files (using B<debsign>(1) to do this instead of B<dpkg-"
"buildpackage>(1) itself; all relevant key-signing options are passed on).  "
"Signing will be skipped if the distribution is I<UNRELEASED>, unless B<dpkg-"
"buildpackage>'s B<--force-sign> option is used.  Parameters can be passed to"
" B<dpkg-buildpackage> and B<lintian>, where the parameters to the latter are"
" indicated with the B<--lintian-opts> option.  The allowable options in this"
" case are B<--lintian> and B<--no-lintian> to force or skip the B<lintian> "
"step, respectively. The default is to run B<lintian>.  There are also "
"various options available for setting and preserving environment variables, "
"as described below in the Environment Variables section.  In this method of "
"running B<debuild>, we also save a build log to the file "
"I<../E<lt>packageE<gt>_E<lt>versionE<gt>_E<lt>archE<gt>.build>."
msgstr ""
"B<debuild> skapar alla filer som behövs för att ladda upp ett Debian-paket. "
"Det kör först B<dpkg-buildpackage>, sedan B<lintian> på den skapade "
"I<.changes>-filen, om B<lintian> är installerat, och signerar slutligen "
"lämpliga filer. Signeringen görs med B<debsign>(1) i stället för med B<dpkg-"
"buildpackage>(1); alla relevanta alternativ för nyckelsignering skickas "
"vidare. Signeringen hoppas över om distributionen är I<UNRELEASED>, såvida "
"inte B<dpkg-buildpackage>-alternativet B<--force-sign> används. Parametrar "
"kan skickas till B<dpkg-buildpackage> och B<lintian>; parametrarna till det "
"senare anges med alternativet B<--lintian-opts>. Alternativen B<--lintian> "
"och B<--no-lintian> kan användas för att tvinga respektive hoppa över steget"
" B<lintian>. Standard är att köra B<lintian>. Det finns också alternativ för"
" att ställa in och bevara miljövariabler, enligt beskrivningen nedan under "
"Miljövariabler. Med denna metod för att köra B<debuild> sparas även en "
"bygglogg i I<../E<lt>packageE<gt>_E<lt>versionE<gt>_E<lt>archE<gt>.build>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:48
msgid ""
"An alternative way of using B<debuild> is to use one or more of the "
"parameters B<binary>, B<binary-arch>, B<binary-indep> and B<clean>, in which"
" case B<debuild> will attempt to gain root privileges and then run "
"I<debian/rules> with the given parameters.  A B<--rootcmd=>I<gain-root-"
"command> or B<-r>I<gain-root-command> option may be used to specify a method"
" of gaining root privileges.  The I<gain-root-command> is likely to be one "
"of I<fakeroot>, I<sudo> or I<super>.  See below for further discussion of "
"this point.  Again, the environment preservation options may be used.  In "
"this case, B<debuild> will also attempt to run B<dpkg-checkbuilddeps> first;"
" this can be explicitly requested or switched off using the options B<-D> "
"and B<-d> respectively.  Note also that if either of these or a B<-r> option"
" is specified in the configuration file option "
"B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS>, then it will be recognised even in this "
"method of invocation of B<debuild>."
msgstr ""
"Ett alternativt sätt att använda B<debuild> är att använda en eller flera av"
" parametrarna B<binary>, B<binary-arch>, B<binary-indep> och B<clean>. Då "
"försöker B<debuild> få rootbehörighet och kör sedan I<debian/rules> med de "
"angivna parametrarna. Alternativen B<--rootcmd=>I<gain-root-command> eller "
"B<-r>I<gain-root-command> kan användas för att ange en metod för att få "
"rootbehörighet. I<gain-root-command> är sannolikt I<fakeroot>, I<sudo> eller"
" I<super>. Se nedan för mer om detta. Alternativen för att bevara miljön kan"
" återigen användas. I detta fall försöker B<debuild> också först köra "
"B<dpkg-checkbuilddeps>; det kan uttryckligen begäras eller stängas av med "
"B<-D> respektive B<-d>. Observera också att om något av dessa eller B<-r> "
"anges i konfigurationsfilalternativet B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS>, "
"känns det igen även med denna metod för att anropa B<debuild>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:51
msgid ""
"B<debuild> also reads the B<devscripts> configuration files as described "
"below.  This allows default options to be given."
msgstr ""
"B<debuild> läser också konfigurationsfilerna B<devscripts> enligt "
"beskrivningen nedan.  Detta gör det möjligt att ange standardalternativ."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:63
msgid ""
"In common with several other scripts in the B<devscripts> package, "
"B<debuild> will climb the directory tree until it finds a "
"I<debian/changelog> file before attempting to build the package.  As a "
"safeguard against stray files causing potential problems, it will examine "
"the name of the parent directory once it finds the I<debian/changelog> file,"
" and check that the directory name corresponds to the package name.  "
"Precisely how it does this is controlled by two configuration file variables"
" B<DEVSCRIPTS_CHECK_DIRNAME_LEVEL> and B<DEVSCRIPTS_CHECK_DIRNAME_REGEX>, "
"and their corresponding command-line options B<--check-dirname-level> and "
"B<--check-dirname-regex>."
msgstr ""
"I likhet med flera andra skript i paketet B<devscripts> går B<debuild> uppåt"
" i katalogträdet tills det hittar en I<debian/changelog>-fil innan det "
"försöker bygga paketet. Som skydd mot ströfiler som kan orsaka problem "
"undersöker det namnet på den överordnade katalogen när det hittar "
"I<debian/changelog>-filen och kontrollerar att katalognamnet motsvarar "
"paketnamnet. Exakt hur detta görs styrs av konfigurationsfilvariablerna "
"B<DEVSCRIPTS_CHECK_DIRNAME_LEVEL> och B<DEVSCRIPTS_CHECK_DIRNAME_REGEX> samt"
" deras motsvarande kommandoradsalternativ B<--check-dirname-level> och "
"B<--check-dirname-regex>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:88
msgid ""
"The directory name is checked by testing whether the current directory name "
"(as determined by B<pwd>(1)) matches the regex given by the configuration "
"file option B<DEVSCRIPTS_CHECK_DIRNAME_REGEX> or by the command line option "
"B<--check-dirname-regex> I<regex>.  Here I<regex> is a Perl regex (see "
"B<perlre>(3perl)), which will be anchored at the beginning and the end.  If "
"I<regex> contains a '/', then it must match the full directory path.  If "
"not, then it must match the full directory name.  If I<regex> contains the "
"string \\(aqPACKAGE', this will be replaced by the source package name, as "
"determined from the I<changelog>.  The default value for the regex is: "
"\\(aqPACKAGE(-.+)?', thus matching directory names such as PACKAGE and "
"PACKAGE-version."
msgstr ""
"Katalognamnet kontrolleras genom att testa om det aktuella katalognamnet, "
"enligt B<pwd>(1), matchar det reguljära uttryck som anges av "
"konfigurationsfilalternativet B<DEVSCRIPTS_CHECK_DIRNAME_REGEX> eller "
"kommandoradsalternativet B<--check-dirname-regex> I<regex>. Här är I<regex> "
"ett reguljärt Perl-uttryck (se B<perlre>(3perl)) som förankras i början och "
"slutet. Om I<regex> innehåller ”/” måste det matcha hela katalogsökvägen. "
"Annars måste det matcha hela katalognamnet. Om I<regex> innehåller strängen "
"(aqPACKAGE’ ersätts den med källpaketets namn enligt I<changelog>. "
"Standardvärdet för regex är (aqPACKAGE(-.+)?’, vilket matchar katalognamn "
"som PACKAGE och PACKAGE-version."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:98
msgid ""
"As environment variables can affect the building of a package, often "
"unintentionally, B<debuild> sanitises the environment by removing all "
"environment variables except for B<TERM>, B<HOME>, B<LOGNAME>, B<GNUPGHOME>,"
" B<PGPPATH>, B<GPG_AGENT_INFO>, B<GPG_TTY>, B<DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS>, "
"B<FAKEROOTKEY>, B<DEBEMAIL>, B<DEB_>I<*>, the (B<C>, B<CPP>, B<CXX>, B<LD> "
"and B<F>)B<FLAGS> variables and their B<_APPEND> counterparts and the locale"
" variables B<LANG> and B<LC_>I<*>.  B<TERM> is set to `dumb' if it is unset,"
" and B<PATH> is set to \"/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/bin/X11\"."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom miljövariabler, ofta oavsiktligt, kan påverka ett paketbygge "
"sanerar B<debuild> miljön genom att ta bort alla miljövariabler utom "
"B<TERM>, B<HOME>, B<LOGNAME>, B<GNUPGHOME>, B<PGPPATH>, B<GPG_AGENT_INFO>, "
"B<GPG_TTY>, B<DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS>, B<FAKEROOTKEY>, B<DEBEMAIL>, "
"B<DEB_>I<*>, variablerna (B<C>, B<CPP>, B<CXX>, B<LD> och B<F>)B<FLAGS> och "
"deras B<_APPEND>-motsvarigheter samt lokalvariablerna B<LANG> och "
"B<LC_>I<*>. B<TERM> sätts till `dumb’ om den saknas, och B<PATH> sätts till "
"”/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/bin/X11”."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:109
msgid ""
"If a particular environment variable is required to be passed through "
"untouched to the build process, this may be specified by using a "
"B<--preserve-envvar> I<envvar> (which can also be written as B<-e> I<envvar>"
" option).  The environment may be left untouched by using the B<--preserve-"
"env> option.  However, even in this case, the B<PATH> will be set to the "
"sane value described above.  The B<only> way to prevent B<PATH> from being "
"reset is to specify a B<--preserve-envvar PATH> option.  But you are warned "
"that using programs from non-standard locations can easily result in the "
"package being broken, as it will not be able to be built on standard "
"systems."
msgstr ""
"Om en viss miljövariabel måste skickas oförändrad till byggprocessen kan det"
" anges med B<--preserve-envvar> I<envvar>, som också kan skrivas som B<-e> "
"I<envvar>. Miljön kan lämnas oförändrad med B<--preserve-env>. Även då sätts"
" B<PATH> till det förnuftiga värde som beskrivs ovan. Det B<enda> sättet att"
" hindra att B<PATH> återställs är att ange B<--preserve-envvar PATH>. Du "
"varnas dock för att program från icke-standardiserade platser lätt kan göra "
"paketet obrukbart, eftersom det då inte kan byggas på standardsystem."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:113
msgid ""
"Note that one may add directories to the beginning of the sanitised B<PATH>,"
" using the B<--prepend-path> option. This is useful when one wishes to use "
"tools such as B<ccache> or B<distcc> for building."
msgstr ""
"Observera att kataloger kan läggas till i början av den sanerade B<PATH> med"
" alternativet B<--prepend-path>. Det är användbart när verktyg som B<ccache>"
" eller B<distcc> ska användas vid bygget."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:118
msgid ""
"It is also possible to avoid having to type something like I<FOO>B<=>I<bar "
">B<debuild -e >I<FOO> by writing B<debuild -e >I<FOO>B<=>I<bar> or the long "
"form B<debuild --set-envvar >I<FOO>B<=>I<bar>."
msgstr ""
"Det är också möjligt att undvika att skriva något som I<FOO>B<=>I<bar "
">B<debuild -e >I<FOO> genom att skriva B<debuild -e >I<FOO>B<=>I<bar> eller "
"den långa formen B<debuild --set-envvar >I<FOO>B<=>I<bar>."

#. type: SH
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "SUPERUSER REQUIREMENTS"
msgstr "KRAV PÅ SUPERANVÄNDARE"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:128
msgid ""
"B<debuild> needs to be run as superuser to function properly.  There are "
"three fundamentally different ways to do this.  The first, and preferable, "
"method is to use some root-gaining command.  The best one to use is probably"
" B<fakeroot>(1), since it does not involve granting any genuine privileges."
"  B<super>(1) and B<sudo>(1) are also possibilities.  If no B<-r> (or "
"B<--rootcmd>) option is given (and recall that B<dpkg-buildpackage> also "
"accepts a B<-r> option) and neither of the following methods is used, then "
"B<-rfakeroot> will silently be assumed."
msgstr ""
"B<debuild> måste köras som superanvändare för att fungera korrekt. Det finns"
" tre fundamentalt olika sätt att göra detta. Den första och lämpligaste "
"metoden är att använda ett kommando för att få rootbehörighet. Troligen är "
"B<fakeroot>(1) bäst eftersom det inte ger några verkliga privilegier. "
"B<super>(1) och B<sudo>(1) är också möjliga. Om inget B<-r>- eller "
"B<--rootcmd>-alternativ anges, och ingen av följande metoder används, antas "
"B<-rfakeroot> tyst. Observera att B<dpkg-buildpackage> också accepterar "
"B<-r>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:134
msgid ""
"The second method is to use some command such as B<su>(1) to become root, "
"and then to do everything as root.  Note, though, that B<lintian> will abort"
" if it is run as root or setuid root; this can be overcome using the "
"B<--allow-root> option of B<lintian> if you know what you are doing."
msgstr ""
"Den andra metoden är att använda ett kommando som B<su>(1) för att bli root "
"och sedan göra allt som root.  Observera dock att B<lintian> avbryts om det "
"körs som root eller setuid root. Detta kan lösas med hjälp av alternativet "
"B<--allow-root> i B<lintian> om du vet vad du gör."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:150
msgid ""
"The third possible method is to have B<debuild> installed as setuid root.  "
"This is not the default method, and will have to be installed as such by the"
" system administrator.  It must also be realised that anyone who can run "
"B<debuild> as root or setuid root has B<full access to the whole machine>.  "
"This method is therefore not recommended, but will work.  B<debuild> could "
"be installed with mode 4754, so that only members of the owning group could "
"run it.  A disadvantage of this method would be that other users would then "
"not be able to use the program.  There are many other variants of this "
"option involving multiple copies of B<debuild>, or the use of programs such "
"as B<sudo> or B<super> to grant root privileges to users selectively.  If "
"the sysadmin wishes to do this, she should use the B<dpkg-statoverride> "
"program to change the permissions of I</usr/bin/debuild>.  This will ensure "
"that these permissions are preserved across upgrades."
msgstr ""
"Den tredje möjliga metoden är att installera B<debuild> som setuid root. Det"
" är inte standard och måste installeras så av systemadministratören. "
"Observera också att den som kan köra B<debuild> som root eller setuid root "
"har B<fullständig åtkomst till hela maskinen>. Metoden rekommenderas därför "
"inte, men fungerar. B<debuild> kan installeras med läge 4754 så att endast "
"medlemmar i ägargruppen kan köra programmet. Nackdelen är att övriga "
"användare då inte kan använda det. Det finns många andra varianter som "
"omfattar flera kopior av B<debuild> eller program som B<sudo> och B<super> "
"för att ge utvalda användare rootbehörighet. Om systemadministratören vill "
"göra detta bör B<dpkg-statoverride> användas för att ändra behörigheterna "
"för I</usr/bin/debuild>, så att de bevaras vid uppgraderingar."

#. type: SH
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "HOOKS"
msgstr "KROKAR"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:156
msgid ""
"B<debuild> supports a number of hooks when running B<dpkg-buildpackage>.  "
"Note that the hooks B<dpkg-buildpackage> to B<lintian> (inclusive) are "
"passed through to B<dpkg-buildpackage> using its corresponding "
"B<--hook->I<name> option.  The available hooks are as follows:"
msgstr ""
"B<debuild> stöder flera krokar när B<dpkg-buildpackage> körs. Krokarna från "
"B<dpkg-buildpackage> till och med B<lintian> skickas vidare till B<dpkg-"
"buildpackage> med motsvarande B<--hook->I<name>-alternativ. Följande krokar "
"är tillgängliga:"

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<dpkg-buildpackage-hook>"
msgstr "B<dpkg-buildpackage-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:159
msgid ""
"Run before B<dpkg-buildpackage> begins by calling B<dpkg-checkbuilddeps>."
msgstr ""
"Kör innan B<dpkg-buildpackage> startar genom att anropa B<dpkg-"
"checkbuilddeps>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:161 ../scripts/debuild.1:170 ../scripts/debuild.1:178
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:187 ../scripts/debuild.1:195 ../scripts/debuild.1:203
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:212
msgid "Hook is run inside the unpacked source."
msgstr "Kroken körs i den uppackade källkoden."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:163
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<init> hook."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<init>-krok."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<clean-hook>"
msgstr "B<clean-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:168
msgid ""
"Run before B<dpkg-buildpackage> runs B<debian/rules clean> to clean the "
"source tree.  (Run even if the tree is not being cleaned because B<-nc> is "
"used.)"
msgstr ""
"Kör före B<dpkg-buildpackage>s B<debian/rules clean> för att rensa "
"källträdet. (Kör även om trädet inte rensas eftersom B<-nc> används.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:172
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<preclean> hook."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<preclean>-krok."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<dpkg-source-hook>"
msgstr "B<dpkg-source-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:176
msgid ""
"Run after cleaning the tree and before running B<dpkg-source>.  (Run even if"
" B<dpkg-source> is not being called because B<-b>, B<-B>, or B<-A> is used.)"
msgstr ""
"Kör efter att trädet har rensats och före B<dpkg-source>. (Kör även om "
"B<dpkg-source> inte anropas eftersom B<-b>, B<-B> eller B<-A> används.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:180
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<source> hook."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<source>-krok."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<dpkg-build-hook>"
msgstr "B<dpkg-build-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:185
msgid ""
"Run after B<dpkg-source> and before calling B<debian/rules build>.  (Run "
"even if this is a source-only build, so B<debian/rules build> is not being "
"called.)"
msgstr ""
"Kör efter B<dpkg-source> och före B<debian/rules build>. (Kör även om bygget"
" endast är ett källkodsbygge och B<debian/rules build> därför inte anropas.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:189
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<build> hook."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<build>-krok."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<dpkg-binary-hook>"
msgstr "B<dpkg-binary-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:193
msgid ""
"Run between B<debian/rules build> and B<debian/rules binary>(B<-arch>).  Run"
" B<only> if a binary package is being built."
msgstr ""
"Kör mellan B<debian/rules build> och B<debian/rules binary>(B<-arch>). Kör "
"B<endast> om ett binärpaket byggs."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:197
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<binary> hook."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<binary>-krok."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<dpkg-genchanges-hook>"
msgstr "B<dpkg-genchanges-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:201
msgid ""
"Run after the binary package is built and before calling B<dpkg-genchanges>."
msgstr "Kör efter att binärpaketet har byggts och före B<dpkg-genchanges>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:205
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<changes> hook."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<changes>-krok."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:205
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<final-clean-hook>"
msgstr "B<final-clean-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:210
msgid ""
"Run after B<dpkg-genchanges> and before the final B<debian/rules clean>.  "
"(Run even if we are not cleaning the tree post-build, which is the default.)"
msgstr ""
"Kör efter B<dpkg-genchanges> och före den slutliga B<debian/rules clean>. "
"(Kör även om trädet inte rensas efter bygget, vilket är standard.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:214
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<postclean> hook."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<postclean>-krok."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<lintian-hook>"
msgstr "B<lintian-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:218
msgid ""
"Run (once) before calling B<lintian>.  (Run even if we are not calling "
"B<lintian>.)"
msgstr "Kör en gång före B<lintian>. (Kör även om B<lintian> inte anropas.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:220 ../scripts/debuild.1:228 ../scripts/debuild.1:235
msgid "Hook is run from parent directory of unpacked source."
msgstr ""
"Kroken körs från den överordnade katalogen till den uppackade källkoden."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:222
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<check> hook."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<check>-krok."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:222
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<signing-hook>"
msgstr "B<signing-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:226
msgid ""
"Run after calling B<lintian> before any signing takes place.  (Run even if "
"we are not signing anything.)"
msgstr ""
"Kör efter B<lintian> men före signering. (Kör även om inget signeras.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:230
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<sign> hook, but is run by B<debuild>."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<sign>-krok, men körs av B<debuild>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:230
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<post-dpkg-buildpackage-hook>"
msgstr "B<post-dpkg-buildpackage-hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:233
msgid "Run after everything has finished."
msgstr "Kör när allt är klart."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:237
msgid "Corresponds to B<dpkg>'s B<done> hook, but is run by B<debuild>."
msgstr "Motsvarar B<dpkg>s B<done>-krok, men körs av B<debuild>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:252
msgid ""
"A hook command can be specified either in the configuration file as, for "
"example, DEBUILD_SIGNING_HOOK='foo' (note the hyphens change into "
"underscores!) or as a command line option B<--signing-hook-foo>.  The "
"command will have certain percent substitutions made on it: B<%%> will be "
"replaced by a single B<%> sign, B<%p> will be replaced by the package name, "
"B<%v> by the package version number, B<%s> by the source version number, "
"B<%u> by the upstream version number.  Neither B<%s> nor B<%u> will contain "
"an epoch.  B<%a> will be B<1> if the immediately following action is to be "
"performed and B<0> if not (for example, in the B<dpkg-source> hook, B<%a> "
"will become B<1> if B<dpkg-source> is to be run and B<0> if not).  Then it "
"will be handed to the shell to deal with, so it can include redirections and"
" stuff.  For example, to only run the B<dpkg-source> hook if B<dpkg-source> "
"is to be run, the hook could be something like: \"if [ %a -eq 1 ]; then ...;"
" fi\"."
msgstr ""
"Ett hook-kommando kan anges antingen i konfigurationsfilen, till exempel "
"DEBUILD_SIGNING_HOOK=’foo’ (bindestreck ändras till understreck), eller som "
"kommandoradsalternativet B<--signing-hook-foo>. Vissa procentersättningar "
"görs i kommandot: B<%%> ersätts med ett B<%>-tecken, B<%p> med paketnamnet, "
"B<%v> med paketets versionsnummer, B<%s> med källversionens nummer och B<%u>"
" med uppströmsversionens nummer. Varken B<%s> eller B<%u> innehåller en "
"epok. B<%a> blir B<1> om den direkt följande åtgärden ska utföras, annars "
"B<0>. I B<dpkg-source>-kroken blir B<%a> till exempel B<1> om B<dpkg-source>"
" ska köras och B<0> annars. Kommandot lämnas sedan till skalet och kan "
"därför innehålla omdirigeringar med mera. För att bara köra B<dpkg-"
"source>-kroken när B<dpkg-source> ska köras kan kroken till exempel vara ”if"
" [ %a -eq 1 ]; then ...; fi”."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:256
msgid ""
"B<Please take care with hooks>, as misuse of them can lead to packages which"
" FTBFS (fail to build from source).  They can be useful for taking snapshots"
" of things or the like."
msgstr ""
"B<Var försiktig med krokar>, eftersom felaktig användning kan leda till "
"paket som FTBFS (inte kan byggas från källkod). De kan vara användbara för "
"att ta ögonblicksbilder eller liknande."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:258
msgid "For details, see above."
msgstr "För mer information, se ovan."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:262
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rootcmd=>I<gain-root-command>, B<-r>I<gain-root-command>"
msgstr "B<--rootcmd=>I<gain-root-command>, B<-r>I<gain-root-command>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:265
msgid "Command to gain root (or fake root) privileges."
msgstr "Kommando för att få root-behörighet (eller falsk root-behörighet)."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:265
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--preserve-env>"
msgstr "B<--preserve-env>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:268
msgid "Do not clean the environment, except for PATH."
msgstr "Rensa inte miljön, utom PATH."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:268
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--preserve-envvar=>I<var>, B<-e>I<var>"
msgstr "B<--preserve-envvar=>I<var>, B<-e>I<var>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:271
msgid "Do not clean the I<var> variable from the environment."
msgstr "Rensa inte bort variabeln I<var> ur miljön."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:275
msgid ""
"If I<var> ends in an asterisk (\"*\") then all variables with names that "
"match the portion of I<var> before the asterisk will be preserved."
msgstr ""
"Om I<var> slutar med en asterisk (\"*\") kommer alla variabler med namn som "
"matchar delen av I<var> före asterisken att bevaras."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:275
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--set-envvar=>I<var>B<=>I<value>, B<-e>I<var>B<=>I<value>"
msgstr "B<--set-envvar=>I<var>B<=>I<value>, B<-e>I<var>B<=>I<value>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:279
msgid ""
"Set the environment variable I<var> to I<value> and do not remove it from "
"the environment."
msgstr ""
"Sätt miljövariabeln I<var> till I<value> och ta inte bort den ur miljön."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:279
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--prepend-path=>I<value >"
msgstr "B<--prepend-path=>I<value >"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:283
msgid "Once the normalized PATH has been set, prepend I<value> to it."
msgstr "När den normaliserade B<PATH> har satts läggs I<value> till före den."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:283
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--lintian>"
msgstr "B<--lintian>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:288
msgid ""
"Run B<lintian> after B<dpkg-buildpackage>.  This is the default behaviour, "
"and it overrides any configuration file directive to the contrary."
msgstr ""
"Kör B<lintian> efter B<dpkg-buildpackage>.  Detta är standardbeteendet och "
"det åsidosätter alla motsatta direktiv i konfigurationsfilen."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:288
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--no-lintian>"
msgstr "B<--no-lintian>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:291
msgid "Do not run B<lintian> after B<dpkg-buildpackage>."
msgstr "Kör inte B<lintian> efter B<dpkg-buildpackage>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:291
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--no-tgz-check>"
msgstr "B<--no-tgz-check>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:296
msgid ""
"Even if we're running B<dpkg-buildpackage> and the version number has a "
"Debian revision, do not check that the I<.orig.tar.gz> file or I<.orig> "
"directory exists before starting the build."
msgstr ""
"Även om B<dpkg-buildpackage> körs och versionsnumret har en Debian-revision,"
" kontrollera inte att filen I<.orig.tar.gz> eller katalogen I<.orig> finns "
"innan bygget startas."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:296
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--tgz-check>"
msgstr "B<--tgz-check>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:301
msgid ""
"If we're running B<dpkg-buildpackage> and the version number has a Debian "
"revision, check that the I<.orig.tar.gz> file or I<.orig> directory exists "
"before starting the build.  This is the default behaviour."
msgstr ""
"Om B<dpkg-buildpackage> körs och versionsnumret har en Debian-revision, "
"kontrollera att filen I<.orig.tar.gz> eller katalogen I<.orig> finns innan "
"bygget startas. Detta är standardbeteendet."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:301
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--username> I<username>"
msgstr "B<--username> I<username>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:305
msgid ""
"When signing, use B<debrsign> instead of B<debsign>.  I<username> specifies "
"the credentials to be used."
msgstr ""
"Använd B<debrsign> i stället för B<debsign> vid signering. I<username> anger"
" vilka autentiseringsuppgifter som ska användas."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:305
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-->I<foo>B<-hook>=I<hook>"
msgstr "B<-->I<foo>B<-hook>=I<hook>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:309
msgid ""
"Set a hook as described above.  If I<hook> is blank, this unsets the hook."
msgstr ""
"Ange en krok enligt beskrivningen ovan. Om I<hook> är tom avaktiveras "
"kroken."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:309
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--clear-hooks>"
msgstr "B<--clear-hooks>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:313
msgid ""
"Clears all hooks.  They may be reinstated by later command line options."
msgstr ""
"Rensar alla krokar. De kan återställas av senare kommandoradsalternativ."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:324
msgid "Do not run B<dpkg-checkbuilddeps> to check build dependencies."
msgstr "Kör inte B<dpkg-checkbuilddeps> för att kontrollera byggberoenden."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:324
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<-D>"
msgstr "B<-D>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:327
msgid "Run B<dpkg-checkbuilddeps> to check build dependencies."
msgstr "Kör B<dpkg-checkbuilddeps> för att kontrollera byggberoenden."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:335
msgid ""
"The two configuration files I</etc/devscripts.conf> and I<~/.devscripts> are"
" sourced by a shell in that order to set configuration variables.  Command "
"line options can be used to override some of these configuration file "
"settings, otherwise the B<--no-conf> option can be used to prevent reading "
"these files.  Environment variable settings are ignored when these "
"configuration files are read.  The currently recognised variables are:"
msgstr ""
"De två konfigurationsfilerna I</etc/devscripts.conf> och I<~/.devscripts> "
"läses in av ett skal i den ordningen för att sätta konfigurationsvariabler. "
"Kommandoradsalternativ kan åsidosätta vissa av dessa inställningar; "
"alternativt kan B<--no-conf> användas för att hindra att filerna läses. "
"Inställningar av miljövariabler ignoreras när konfigurationsfilerna läses. "
"Följande variabler stöds för närvarande:"

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:335
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_PRESERVE_ENV>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_PRESERVE_ENV>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:339
msgid ""
"If this is set to I<yes>, then it is the same as the B<--preserve-env> "
"command line parameter being used."
msgstr ""
"Om detta är inställt på I<yes>, är det samma sak som att "
"kommandoradsparametern B<--preserve-env> används."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:339
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_PRESERVE_ENVVARS>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_PRESERVE_ENVVARS>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:344
msgid ""
"Which environment variables to preserve.  This should be a comma-separated "
"list of variables.  This corresponds to using possibly multiple "
"B<--preserve-envvar> or B<-e> options."
msgstr ""
"Anger vilka miljövariabler som ska bevaras. Detta ska vara en kommaseparerad"
" lista med variabler. Det motsvarar användning av ett eller flera alternativ"
" B<--preserve-envvar> eller B<-e>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:344
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_SET_ENVVAR_>I<var>B<=>I<value>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_SET_ENVVAR_>I<var>B<=>I<value>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:347
msgid "This corresponds to B<--set-envvar=>I<var>B<=>I<value>."
msgstr "Detta motsvarar B<--set-envvar=>I<var>B<=>I<value>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:347
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_PREPEND_PATH>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_PREPEND_PATH>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:350
msgid "This corresponds to B<--prepend-path>."
msgstr "Detta motsvarar B<--prepend-path>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:350
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_ROOTCMD>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_ROOTCMD>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:354
msgid "Setting this variable to I<prog> is the equivalent of B<-r>I<prog>."
msgstr "Att ställa in denna variabel till I<prog> motsvarar B<-r>I<prog>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:354
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_TGZ_CHECK>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_TGZ_CHECK>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:358
msgid ""
"Setting this variable to I<no> is the same as the B<--no-tgz-check> command "
"line option."
msgstr ""
"Att ställa in denna variabel till I<no> är detsamma som "
"kommandoradsalternativet B<--no-tgz-check>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:358
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_SIGNING_USERNAME>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_SIGNING_USERNAME>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:362
msgid ""
"Setting this variable is the same as using the B<--username> command line "
"option."
msgstr ""
"Att ställa in denna variabel är detsamma som att använda "
"kommandoradsalternativet B<--username>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:362
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:370
msgid ""
"These are options which should be passed to the invocation of B<dpkg-"
"buildpackage>.  They are given before any command-line options.  Due to "
"issues of shell quoting, if a word containing spaces is required as a single"
" option, extra quotes will be required.  For example, to ensure that your "
"own GPG key is always used, even for sponsored uploads, the configuration "
"file might contain the line:"
msgstr ""
"Detta är alternativ som ska skickas till anropet av B<dpkg-buildpackage>. De"
" anges före alla kommandoradsalternativ. På grund av skalets citeringsregler"
" krävs extra citattecken om ett ord med mellanslag ska utgöra ett enda "
"alternativ. För att till exempel säkerställa att den egna GPG-nyckeln alltid"
" används, även vid sponsrade uppladdningar, kan konfigurationsfilen "
"innehålla raden:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:373
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS=\"-k'Julian Gilbey E<lt>jdg@debian.orgE<gt>' "
"-sa\"\n"
msgstr ""
"DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS=\"-k'Julian Gilbey E<lt>jdg@debian.orgE<gt>' "
"-sa\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:378
msgid ""
"which gives precisely two options.  Without the extra single quotes, B<dpkg-"
"buildpackage> would reasonably complain that I<Gilbey> is an unrecognised "
"option (it doesn't start with a B<-> sign)."
msgstr ""
"vilket ger exakt två alternativ. Utan de extra enkla citattecknen skulle "
"B<dpkg-buildpackage> rimligen klaga på att I<Gilbey> är ett okänt "
"alternativ, eftersom det inte börjar med B<->."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:383
msgid ""
"Also, if this option contains any B<-r>, B<-d> or B<-D> options, these will "
"always be taken account of by B<debuild>.  Note that a B<-r> option in this "
"variable will override the setting in B<DEBUILD_ROOTCMD>."
msgstr ""
"Om denna variabel dessutom innehåller alternativ B<-r>, B<-d> eller B<-D> "
"beaktas de alltid av B<debuild>. Observera att ett B<-r>-alternativ i "
"variabeln åsidosätter inställningen i B<DEBUILD_ROOTCMD>."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:383
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_>I<FOO>B<_HOOK>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_>I<FOO>B<_HOOK>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:387
msgid ""
"The hook variable for the I<foo> hook.  See the section on hooks above for "
"more details.  By default, this is empty."
msgstr ""
"Krokvariabeln för kroken I<foo>. Se avsnittet om krokar ovan för mer "
"information. Standardvärdet är tomt."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:387
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_LINTIAN>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_LINTIAN>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:391
msgid ""
"Should we run B<lintian>? If this is set to I<no>, then B<lintian> will not "
"be run."
msgstr ""
"Ska vi köra B<lintian>? Om detta är inställt på I<no>, kommer B<lintian> "
"inte att köras."

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:391
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<DEBUILD_LINTIAN_OPTS>"
msgstr "B<DEBUILD_LINTIAN_OPTS>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:397
msgid ""
"These are options which should be passed to the invocation of B<lintian>.  "
"They are given before any command-line options, and the usage of this "
"variable is as described for the B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS> variable."
msgstr ""
"Detta är alternativ som ska skickas till anropet av B<lintian>. De anges "
"före alla kommandoradsalternativ, och variabeln används enligt beskrivningen"
" för B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:408
msgid ""
"To build your own package, simply run B<debuild> from inside the source "
"tree.  B<dpkg-buildpackage>(1) options may be given on the command line."
msgstr ""
"För att bygga ett eget paket kör du bara B<debuild> från källträdet. "
"Alternativ till B<dpkg-buildpackage>(1) kan anges på kommandoraden."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:411
msgid ""
"The typical command line options to build only the binary package(s)  "
"without signing the .changes file (or the non-existent .dsc file):"
msgstr ""
"De typiska kommandoradsalternativen för att enbart bygga binärpaket utan att"
" signera .changes-filen, eller den obefintliga .dsc-filen:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:414
#, no-wrap
msgid "debuild -i -us -uc -b\n"
msgstr "debuild -i -us -uc -b\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:417
msgid "Change the B<-b> to B<-S> to build only a source package."
msgstr "Ändra B<-b> till B<-S> för att endast bygga ett källpaket."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:420
msgid ""
"An example using B<lintian> to check the resulting packages and passing "
"options to it:"
msgstr ""
"Ett exempel som använder B<lintian> för att kontrollera de resulterande "
"paketen och skickar alternativ till det:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:423
#, no-wrap
msgid "debuild --lintian-opts -i\n"
msgstr "debuild --lintian-opts -i\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:431
msgid ""
"Note the order of options here: the B<debuild> options come first, then the "
"B<dpkg-buildpackage> ones, then finally the checker options.  (And "
"B<lintian> is called by default.)  If you find yourself using the same "
"B<dpkg-buildpackage> options repeatedly, consider using the "
"B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS> configuration file option as described "
"above."
msgstr ""
"Observera alternativens ordning: först kommer B<debuild>-alternativen, sedan"
" alternativen till B<dpkg-buildpackage> och sist alternativen till "
"kontrollprogrammet. (B<lintian> anropas som standard.) Om du återkommande "
"använder samma alternativ till B<dpkg-buildpackage> bör du överväga "
"konfigurationsfilalternativet B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS> som beskrivs"
" ovan."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:435
msgid ""
"To build a package for a sponsored upload, given I<foobar_1.0-1.dsc> and the"
" respective source files, run something like the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"För att bygga ett paket för en sponsrad uppladdning, med I<foobar_1.0-1.dsc>"
" och tillhörande källfiler, kör du till exempel:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:440
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"dpkg-source -x foobar_1.0-1.dsc\n"
"cd foobar-1.0\n"
"debuild -k0x12345678\n"
msgstr ""
"dpkg-source -x foobar_1.0-1.dsc\n"
"cd foobar-1.0\n"
"debuild -k0x12345678\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:447
msgid ""
"where 0x12345678 is replaced by your GPG key ID or other key identifier such"
" as your email address.  Again, you could also use the "
"B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS> configuration file option as described "
"above to avoid having to type the B<-k> option each time you do a sponsored "
"upload."
msgstr ""
"där 0x12345678 ersätts med ditt GPG-nyckel-ID eller en annan "
"nyckelidentifierare, till exempel din e-postadress. Du kan även använda "
"konfigurationsfilalternativet B<DEBUILD_DPKG_BUILDPACKAGE_OPTS> enligt "
"beskrivningen ovan för att slippa ange B<-k> vid varje sponsrad uppladdning."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:459
msgid ""
"B<chmod>(1), B<debsign>(1), B<dpkg-buildpackage>(1), B<dpkg-"
"checkbuilddeps>(1), B<fakeroot>(1), B<lintian>(1), B<su>(1), B<sudo>(1), "
"B<super>(1), B<devscripts.conf>(5), B<dpkg-statoverride>(8)"
msgstr ""
"B<chmod>(1), B<debsign>(1), B<dpkg-buildpackage>(1), B<dpkg-"
"checkbuilddeps>(1), B<fakeroot>(1), B<lintian>(1), B<su>(1), B<sudo>(1), "
"B<super>(1), B<devscripts.conf>(5), B<dpkg-statoverride>(8)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/debuild.1:462
msgid ""
"The original B<debuild> program was written by Christoph Lameter "
"E<lt>clameter@debian.orgE<gt>.  The current version has been written by "
"Julian Gilbey E<lt>jdg@debian.orgE<gt>."
msgstr ""
"Det ursprungliga programmet B<debuild> skrevs av Christoph Lameter "
"E<lt>clameter@debian.orgE<gt>. Den nuvarande versionen skrevs av Julian "
"Gilbey E<lt>jdg@debian.orgE<gt>."

#. type: TH
#: ../scripts/dep3changelog.1:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEP3CHANGELOG"
msgstr "DEP3CHANGELOG"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep3changelog.1:4
msgid ""
"dep3changelog - generate a changelog entry from a DEP3-style patch header"
msgstr ""
"dep3changelog – skapa en post i ändringsloggen från ett patchhuvud i "
"DEP3-format"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep3changelog.1:6
msgid ""
"B<dep3changelog> I<patch> [I<patch> ...] [I<options>] [-- [I<dch_options>]]"
msgstr ""
"B<dep3changelog> I<patch> [I<patch> ...] [I<options>] [-- [I<dch_options>]]"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep3changelog.1:15
msgid ""
"B<dep3changelog> extracts the DEP3 patch headers from the given I<patch> "
"files and builds a changelog entry for each patch.  If the patch author "
"differs from the one detected from the B<DEBEMAIL>, B<NAME>, B<DEBEMAIL>, or"
" B<EMAIL> environment variables, ``Thanks to I<author> E<lt>I<email>E<gt>'' "
"is added to the changelog entry for that patch.  Any B<bug-debian> or B<bug-"
"ubuntu> fields are added as ``Closes'' to the changelog entry.  The "
"generated changelog entries are passed to B<debchange> as an argument along "
"with the given I<dch_options>."
msgstr ""
"B<dep3changelog> extraherar DEP3-patchhuvuden från angivna I<patch>-filer "
"och skapar en post i ändringsloggen för varje patch. Om patchförfattaren "
"skiljer sig från den som identifieras genom miljövariablerna B<DEBEMAIL>, "
"B<NAME>, B<DEBEMAIL> eller B<EMAIL> läggs ”Thanks to I<author> "
"E<lt>I<email>E<gt>” till i patchens post i ändringsloggen. Fält B<bug-"
"debian> och B<bug-ubuntu> läggs till som ”Closes”. De skapade posterna "
"skickas som argument till B<debchange> tillsammans med angivna "
"I<dch_options>."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep3changelog.1:28
msgid "Steve Langasek E<lt>vorlon@debian.orgE<gt>"
msgstr "Steve Langasek E<lt>vorlon@debian.orgE<gt>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep3changelog.1:29 ../scripts/list-unreleased.1:21
msgid "B<debchange>(1)"
msgstr "B<debchange>(1)"

#. type: TH
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEP-14-CONVERT-GIT-BRANCH-NAMES"
msgstr "DEP-14-CONVERT-GIT-BRANCH-NAMES"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:4
msgid ""
"dep-14-convert-git-branch-names - Convert git repository branch names to "
"follow DEP-14."
msgstr ""
"dep-14-convert-git-branch-names – konvertera grennamn i ett gitarkiv så att "
"de följer DEP-14."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:9
msgid ""
"This helper tool assists in renaming the branch names by printing the "
"necessary git commands for local repository and salsa commands remote "
"repository to rename the branches and to update the default git branch. It "
"also prints commands to create a gbp.conf with matching branch names."
msgstr ""
"Hjälpverktyget underlättar namnbyte av grenar genom att skriva ut de git-"
"kommandon som behövs för lokala arkiv och Salsa-kommandon för fjärrarkiv. "
"Kommandona byter namn på grenarna och uppdaterar standardgrenen i git. "
"Verktyget skriver också ut kommandon för att skapa en gbp.conf med "
"motsvarande grennamn."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:12
msgid ""
"As this script does not actually modify anything, so feel free to run this "
"script in any Debian packaging repository to see what it outputs."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom detta skript inte ändrar något, kan du köra det i valfritt Debian-"
"paketarkiv för att se vad det ger för resultat."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:17
msgid ""
"Renaming is needed as git defaults to 'main' as the branch name. Previously "
"git used 'master', and git-buildpackage still used 'master' as the branch "
"name. This is not ideal for Debian packaging, as using the same default "
"development branch names as upstream projects typically do may lead into "
"branch name conflicts."
msgstr ""
"Namnbyte behövs eftersom git som standard använder ”main” som grennamn. "
"Tidigare använde git ”master”, och git-buildpackage använde fortfarande "
"”master”. Det är inte idealiskt för Debian-paketering, eftersom samma "
"standardnamn på utvecklingsgrenar som uppströmsprojekt normalt använder kan "
"leda till konflikter mellan grennamn."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:20
msgid ""
"The DEP-14 (https://dep-team.pages.debian.net/deps/dep14/, status: "
"candidate)  states:"
msgstr ""
"DEP-14 (https://dep-team.pages.debian.net/deps/dep14/, status: candidate) "
"anger:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In Debian this means that uploads to unstable and experimental should be\n"
"  prepared either in the debian/latest branch or respectively in the\n"
"  debian/unstable and debian/experimental branches.\n"
msgstr ""
"  In Debian this means that uploads to unstable and experimental should be\n"
"  prepared either in the debian/latest branch or respectively in the\n"
"  debian/unstable and debian/experimental branches.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:26
msgid "and:"
msgstr "och:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:30
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The helper tools that do create those repositories should use a command like\n"
"  git symbolic-ref HEAD refs/heads/debian/latest to update HEAD to point to the\n"
"  desired branch.\n"
msgstr ""
"  The helper tools that do create those repositories should use a command like\n"
"  git symbolic-ref HEAD refs/heads/debian/latest to update HEAD to point to the\n"
"  desired branch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:33
msgid "B<dep-14-convert-git-branch-names> [I<\\,options\\/>]"
msgstr "B<dep-14-convert-git-branch-names> [I<\\,options\\/>]"

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options:"
msgstr "Alternativ:"

#. type: TP
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--packaging-branch> E<lt>nameE<gt>"
msgstr "B<--packaging-branch> E<lt>nameE<gt>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:39
msgid "Branch for main packaging (e.g. 'debian/latest')"
msgstr "Gren för huvudpaketeringen (t.ex. ”debian/latest”)"

#. type: =item
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:39
#: ../scripts/grep-excuses.1:43 ../scripts/hardening-check.pl:671
#: ../scripts/salsa.pl:568
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--debug>"
msgstr "B<--debug>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:42
msgid "Display debug information while running"
msgstr "Visa felsökningsinformation under körningen"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:45
msgid "Display this help message"
msgstr "Visa detta hjälpmeddelande"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:48
msgid "Display version information"
msgstr "Visa versionsinformation"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../scripts/dep-14-convert-git-branch-names.1:49
msgid "DEP-14: https://dep-team.pages.debian.net/deps/dep14/"
msgstr "DEP-14: https://dep-team.pages.debian.net/deps/dep14/"

#. type: TH
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEVSCRIPTS"
msgstr "DEVSCRIPTS"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:4
msgid "devscripts - scripts to ease the lives of Debian developers"
msgstr "devscripts – skript som underlättar livet för Debian-utvecklare"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:12
msgid ""
"The B<devscripts> package provides a collection of scripts which may be of "
"use to Debian developers and others wishing to build Debian packages.  For a"
" summary of the available scripts, please see the file "
"I</usr/share/doc/devscripts/README.gz>, and for full details, please see the"
" individual manpages.  They are contributed by multiple developers; for "
"details of the authors, please see the code or manpages."
msgstr ""
"Paketet B<devscripts> innehåller en samling skript som kan vara till nytta "
"för Debian-utvecklare och andra som vill bygga Debian-paket. En "
"sammanfattning av tillgängliga skript finns i "
"I</usr/share/doc/devscripts/README.gz>; fullständig information finns i "
"respektive manualsida. Flera utvecklare har bidragit; se koden eller "
"manualsidorna för uppgifter om författarna."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:16
msgid ""
"Also, the directory I</usr/share/doc/devscripts/examples> contains an "
"example B<exim> script for sorting mail arriving to Debian mailing lists."
msgstr ""
"Katalogen I</usr/share/doc/devscripts/examples> innehåller också ett exempel"
" på ett B<exim>-skript för att sortera e-post som kommer till Debians "
"e-postlistor."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:20
msgid ""
"Several scripts of the devscripts suite use the following environment "
"variables. Check the man pages of individual scripts for more details on how"
" the variables are used."
msgstr ""
"Flera skript i sviten devscripts använder följande miljövariabler. Se "
"respektive manualsida för mer information om hur variablerna används."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\s-1DEBEMAIL\\s0"
msgstr "\\s-1DEBEMAIL\\s0"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:22
msgid "Email of the person acting on a given Debian package via devscripts."
msgstr ""
"E-postadress till den person som hanterar ett visst Debian-paket via "
"devscripts."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\s-1DEBFULLNAME\\s0"
msgstr "\\s-1DEBFULLNAME\\s0"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:25
msgid ""
"Full name (first + family) of the person acting on a given Debian package "
"via devscripts."
msgstr ""
"Fullständigt namn, förnamn och efternamn, på personen som hanterar ett visst"
" Debian-paket via devscripts."

#. type: SH
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "SCRIPTS"
msgstr "SKRIPT"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:28
msgid ""
"Here is the complete list of available devscripts. See their man pages for "
"additional documentation."
msgstr ""
"Här är den fullständiga listan över tillgängliga skript i devscripts. Se "
"deras manualsidor för ytterligare dokumentation."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<annotate-output>(1)"
msgstr "I<annotate-output>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:30
msgid ""
"run a command and prepend time and stream (O for stdout, E for stderr) for "
"every line of output."
msgstr ""
"Kör ett kommando och lägg till tid och ström, O för stdout och E för stderr,"
" före varje utmatningsrad."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<archpath>(1)"
msgstr "I<archpath>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:32
msgid ""
"Prints arch (tla/Bazaar 1.x) package names. Also supports calculating the "
"package names for other branches. [tla]"
msgstr ""
"Skriver ut paketnamn för arch (tla/Bazaar 1.x). Stöder även beräkning av "
"paketnamn för andra grenar. [tla]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<bts>(1)"
msgstr "I<bts>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:34
msgid ""
"Comprehensive CLI for the Debian Bug Tracking System (BTS). Supports 1) "
"reading and finding bugs in CLI email clients (MUAs) or a web-browser, 2) "
"changing bugs non-interactively, 3) submitting and replying to bugs "
"efficiently from your shell or MUA and finally 4) fetching bug information "
"directly from the BTS SOAP interface. [www-browser, libauthen-sasl-perl, "
"libsoap-lite-perl, liburi-perl, libwww-perl, default-mta | mail-transport-"
"agent]"
msgstr ""
"Omfattande CLI för Debian Bug Tracking System (BTS). Stöder 1) läsning och "
"sökning efter fel i CLI-e-postklienter (MUA) eller en webbläsare, 2) icke-"
"interaktiv ändring av fel, 3) effektiv insändning av och svar på fel från "
"ditt skal eller din MUA samt 4) direkt hämtning av felinformation från BTS "
"SOAP-gränssnitt. [www-browser, libauthen-sasl-perl, libsoap-lite-perl, "
"liburi-perl, libwww-perl, default-mta | mail-transport-agent]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<build-rdeps>(1)"
msgstr "I<build-rdeps>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:36
msgid ""
"Searches for all packages that build-depend on a given package. [dctrl-"
"tools, dose-extra, libdpkg-perl]"
msgstr ""
"Söker efter alla paket som är byggberoende av ett angivet paket. [dctrl-"
"tools, dose-extra, libdpkg-perl]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<chdist>(1)"
msgstr "I<chdist>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:38
msgid "tool to easily play with several distributions. [dctrl-tools]"
msgstr "verktyg för att enkelt testa flera distributioner. [dctrl-tools]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<checkbashisms>(1)"
msgstr "I<checkbashisms>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:40
msgid ""
"check whether a /bin/sh script contains any common bash-specific constructs."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollerar om ett /bin/sh-skript innehåller vanliga bashspecifika "
"konstruktioner."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<cowpoke>(1)"
msgstr "I<cowpoke>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:42
msgid ""
"upload a Debian source package to a cowbuilder host and build it, optionally"
" also signing and uploading the result to an incoming queue. [ssh-client]"
msgstr ""
"Laddar upp ett Debian-källpaket till en cowbuilder-värd och bygger det; "
"resultatet kan även signeras och laddas upp till en inkommande kö. [ssh-"
"client]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<dcmd>(1)"
msgstr "I<dcmd>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:44
msgid ""
"run a given command replacing the name of a .changes or .dsc file with each "
"of the files referenced therein. *"
msgstr ""
"Kör ett angivet kommando och ersätter namnet på en .changes- eller .dsc-fil "
"med var och en av filerna som filen hänvisar till. *"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<dd-list>(1)"
msgstr "I<dd-list>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:46
msgid "given a list of packages, pretty-print it ordered by maintainer. *"
msgstr ""
"Tar en lista med paket och skriver ut den snyggt, sorterad efter ansvarig. *"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debbisect>(1)"
msgstr "I<debbisect>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:48
msgid ""
"bisect snapshot.debian.org to find which change in the archive introduced a "
"certain problem. [debvm, mmdebstrap, python3-debian]"
msgstr ""
"Bisekterar snapshot.debian.org för att hitta vilken ändring i arkivet som "
"introducerade ett visst problem. [debvm, mmdebstrap, python3-debian]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debc>(1)"
msgstr "I<debc>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:50
msgid ""
"List contents of current package.  Do this after a successful \"debuild\" to"
" see if the package looks all right."
msgstr ""
"Lista innehållet i det aktuella paketet. Gör detta efter en lyckad "
"\"debuild\" för att se om paketet ser bra ut."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debchange (abbreviation dch)>(1)"
msgstr "I<debchange (förkortning dch)>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:52
msgid ""
"Modifies debian/changelog and manages version numbers for you.  It will "
"either increment the version number or add an entry for the current version,"
" depending upon the options given to it. [libdistro-info-perl, libsoap-lite-"
"perl]*"
msgstr ""
"Ändrar debian/changelog och hanterar versionsnummer. Beroende på angivna "
"alternativ höjer den antingen versionsnumret eller lägger till en post för "
"den aktuella versionen. [libdistro-info-perl, libsoap-lite-perl]*"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debcheckout>(1)"
msgstr "I<debcheckout>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:54
msgid "checkout the development repository of a Debian package. *"
msgstr "Checkar ut utvecklingsarkivet för ett Debian-paket. *"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debclean>(1)"
msgstr "I<debclean>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:56
msgid ""
"Clean a Debian source tree.  Debclean will clean all Debian source trees "
"below the current directory, and if requested, also remove all files that "
"were generated from these source trees (that is .deb, .dsc and .changes "
"files).  It will keep the .diffs and original files, though, so that the "
"binaries and other files can be rebuilt if necessary. *"
msgstr ""
"Rensa ett Debian-källkodsträd. Debclean rensar alla Debian-källkodsträd "
"under den aktuella katalogen och tar på begäran även bort alla filer som "
"genererats från dessa källkodsträd (det vill säga .deb-, .dsc- och .changes-"
"filer). Det behåller dock .diff-filerna och originalfilerna så att "
"binärfilerna och andra filer kan byggas om vid behov. *"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debcommit>(1)"
msgstr "I<debcommit>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:58
msgid ""
"Commits changes to cvs, darcs, svn, svk, tla, bzr, git, or hg, using new "
"entries in debian/changelog as the commit message. Also supports tagging "
"Debian package releases. [cvs | darcs | subversion | svk | tla | bzr | git-"
"core | mercurial, libtimedate-perl]"
msgstr ""
"Checkar in ändringar i cvs, darcs, svn, svk, tla, bzr, git eller hg och "
"använder nya poster i debian/changelog som incheckningsmeddelande. Stöder "
"även taggning av Debian-paketutgåvor. [cvs | darcs | subversion | svk | tla "
"| bzr | git-core | mercurial, libtimedate-perl]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debdiff>(1)"
msgstr "I<debdiff>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:60
msgid ""
"A program which examines two .deb files or two .changes files and reports on"
" any difference found in their file lists.  Useful for ensuring that no "
"files were inadvertently lost between versions.  Can also examine two .dsc "
"files and report on the changes between source versions. For a deeper "
"comparison one can use the diffoscope package. [wdiff, patchutils]*"
msgstr ""
"Ett program som undersöker två .deb-filer eller två .changes-filer och "
"rapporterar eventuella skillnader i deras fillistor. Användbart för att "
"säkerställa att inga filer oavsiktligt har gått förlorade mellan "
"versionerna. Kan också undersöka två .dsc-filer och rapportera om "
"skillnaderna mellan källversionerna. För en mer ingående jämförelse kan man "
"använda paketet diffoscope. [wdiff, patchutils]*"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debdiff-apply>(1)"
msgstr "I<debdiff-apply>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:62
msgid ""
"Apply unified diffs of two Debian source packages, such as those generated "
"by debdiff, to a target Debian source package. Any changes to "
"debian/changelog are dealt with specially, to avoid the conflicts that "
"changelog diffs typically produce when applied naively. May be used to check"
" that old patches still apply to newer versions of those packages. "
"[python3-debian, python3-unidiff, quilt]"
msgstr ""
"Tillämpar enhetliga diffar mellan två Debian-källpaket, till exempel sådana "
"som skapats av debdiff, på ett Debian-källpaket som mål. Ändringar i "
"debian/changelog hanteras särskilt för att undvika de konflikter som diffar "
"för ändringsloggen normalt orsakar vid naiv tillämpning. Kan användas för "
"att kontrollera att gamla patchar fortfarande kan tillämpas på nyare "
"versioner av paketen. [python3-debian, python3-unidiff, quilt]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debftbfs>(1)"
msgstr "I<debftbfs>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:64
msgid ""
"list source packages which have FTBFS bugs filed against them and print them"
" with the bug number and title. [postgresql-client, python3-debian, "
"python3-debianbts]"
msgstr ""
"lista källpaket som har FTBFS-fel rapporterade mot dem och skriv ut dem med "
"felnummer och titel. [postgresql-client, python3-debian, python3-debianbts]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debi>(1)"
msgstr "I<debi>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:66
msgid ""
"Installs the current package by using dpkg.  It assumes that the current "
"package has just been built (for example by debuild), and the .deb lives in "
"the parent directory, and will effectively run dpkg -i on the .deb. The "
"ability to install the package with a very short command is very useful when"
" troubleshooting packages."
msgstr ""
"Installerar det aktuella paketet med dpkg. Det förutsätter att paketet just "
"har byggts, till exempel med debuild, och att .deb-filen ligger i den "
"överordnade katalogen; i praktiken körs dpkg -i på .deb-filen. Möjligheten "
"att installera paketet med ett mycket kort kommando är användbar vid "
"felsökning. "

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debootsnap>(1)"
msgstr "I<debootsnap>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:68
msgid ""
"Combines debootstrap and snapshot.debian.org to create a chroot containing "
"exactly the requested selection of packages. This can be used to re-create a"
" chroot from the past, for example to reproduce a bug. The tool is also used"
" by debrebuild to build a package in a chroot with build dependencies in the"
" same version as recorded in the buildinfo file. [apt-utils, equivs, "
"mmdebstrap, python3-debian, python3-pycurl, python3-requests]"
msgstr ""
"Kombinerar debootstrap och snapshot.debian.org för att skapa en chroot med "
"exakt det begärda paketurvalet. Detta kan användas för att återskapa en "
"tidigare chroot, till exempel för att återskapa ett fel. Verktyget används "
"också av debrebuild för att bygga ett paket i en chroot där byggberoendena "
"har samma version som i buildinfo-filen. [apt-utils, equivs, mmdebstrap, "
"python3-debian, python3-pycurl, python3-requests]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debrelease>(1)"
msgstr "I<debrelease>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:70
msgid ""
"A wrapper around dupload or dput which figures out which version to upload, "
"and then calls dupload or dput to actually perform the upload. [dupload | "
"dput, ssh-client]"
msgstr ""
"Ett omslag kring dupload eller dput som avgör vilken version som ska laddas "
"upp och sedan anropar dupload eller dput för själva uppladdningen. [dupload "
"| dput, ssh-client]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debrebuild>(1)"
msgstr "I<debrebuild>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:72
msgid ""
"Given a buildinfo file, builds the referenced source package in an "
"environment documented in the provided buildinfo file. The build can be "
"performed by sbuild or other builders in a chroot environment created by "
"debootsnap. The generated artifacts will be verified against the hashes from"
" the buildinfo file. [sbuild | mmdebstrap, python3-pycurl, libdpkg-perl, "
"libstring-shellquote-perl]"
msgstr ""
"Med en buildinfo-fil bygger verktyget det refererade källpaketet i en miljö "
"som dokumenteras i den tillhandahållna buildinfo-filen. Bygget kan utföras "
"av sbuild eller andra byggverktyg i en chroot-miljö som skapats av "
"debootsnap. De skapade artefakterna verifieras mot hashvärdena i buildinfo-"
"filen. [sbuild | mmdebstrap, python3-pycurl, libdpkg-perl, libstring-"
"shellquote-perl]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debrepro>(1)"
msgstr "I<debrepro>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:74
msgid ""
"A script that tests reproducibility of Debian packages. It will build a "
"given source directory twice, with a set of variation between the first and "
"second build, and compare the binary packages produced. If diffoscope is "
"installed, it is used to compare non-matching binaries. If disorderfs is "
"installed, it is used during the build to inject non-determinism in "
"filesystem listing operations. [faketime, diffoscope, disorderfs]"
msgstr ""
"Ett skript som testar reproducerbarheten hos Debian-paket. Det bygger en "
"given källkatalog två gånger, med variationer mellan den första och andra "
"byggkörningen, och jämför de skapade binärpaketen. Om diffoscope är "
"installerat används det för att jämföra binärer som inte matchar. Om "
"disorderfs är installerat används det under bygget för att införa icke-"
"determinism i filsystemets listningsoperationer. [faketime, diffoscope, "
"disorderfs]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debrsign>(1)"
msgstr "I<debrsign>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:76
msgid ""
"This transfers a .changes/.dsc pair to a remote machine for signing, and "
"runs debsign on the remote machine over an SSH connection. [gnupg, debian-"
"keyring, ssh-client]"
msgstr ""
"För över ett .changes/.dsc-par till en fjärrdator för signering och kör "
"debsign där via SSH. [gnupg, debian-keyring, ssh-client]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debsign>(1)"
msgstr "I<debsign>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:78
msgid ""
"Use GNU Privacy Guard to sign the changes (and possibly dsc) files created "
"by running dpkg-buildpackage with no-sign options.  Useful if you are "
"building a package on a remote machine and wish to sign it on a local one.  "
"This script is capable of automatically downloading the .changes and .dsc "
"files from a remote machine. [gnupg, debian-keyring, ssh-client]*"
msgstr ""
"Använder GNU Privacy Guard för att signera .changes-filerna, och eventuellt "
".dsc-filerna, som skapats av dpkg-buildpackage med alternativ utan "
"signering. Användbart om du bygger ett paket på en fjärrdator och vill "
"signera det lokalt. Skriptet kan automatiskt hämta .changes- och .dsc-filer "
"från en fjärrdator. [gnupg, debian-keyring, ssh-client]*"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debsnap>(1)"
msgstr "I<debsnap>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:80
msgid ""
"grab packages from https://snapshot.debian.org [libwww-perl, libjson-perl]"
msgstr ""
"hämta paket från https://snapshot.debian.org [libwww-perl, libjson-perl]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<debuild>(1)"
msgstr "I<debuild>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:82
msgid ""
"A wrapper for building a package (i.e., dpkg-buildpackage) to avoid problems"
" with insufficient permissions and wrong paths etc. Debuild will set up the "
"proper environment for building a package. Debuild will also run lintian to "
"check that the package does not have any major policy violations. [lintian, "
"gnupg]*"
msgstr ""
"Ett omslag för att bygga ett paket, det vill säga dpkg-buildpackage, som "
"undviker problem med otillräckliga behörigheter och felaktiga sökvägar. "
"Debuild ställer in rätt miljö för paketbygget och kör även lintian för att "
"kontrollera att paketet saknar större policyöverträdelser. [lintian, gnupg]*"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<deb-check-file-conflicts>(1)"
msgstr "I<deb-check-file-conflicts>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:84
msgid ""
"Check (using apt-file) if a Debian package installs files in the exact same "
"path as any other package, and if there are Breaks/Replaces (or Conflicts) "
"defined in debian/control to avoid the package installation failing on file "
"conflicts."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollerar med apt-file om ett Debian-paket installerar filer på exakt "
"samma sökväg som något annat paket och om Breaks/Replaces, eller Conflicts, "
"är definierade i debian/control för att undvika att paketinstallationen "
"misslyckas på grund av filkonflikter."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<deb-janitor>(1)"
msgstr "I<deb-janitor>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:86
msgid "command-line client for interacting with the Debian Janitor."
msgstr "Kommandoradsklient för att interagera med Debian Janitor."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<deb-reversion>(1)"
msgstr "I<deb-reversion>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:88
msgid ""
"increases a binary package version number and repacks the package, useful "
"for porters and the like."
msgstr ""
"Ökar versionsnumret för ett binärpaket och packar om paketet, vilket är "
"användbart för portare och liknande."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<deb-why-removed>(1)"
msgstr "I<deb-why-removed>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:90
msgid ""
"shows the reason a package was removed from the archive. [libdpkg-perl]"
msgstr ""
"visar anledningen till att ett paket har tagits bort från arkivet. [libdpkg-"
"perl]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<deb2apptainer>(1)"
msgstr "I<deb2apptainer>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:92
msgid "build a Singularity/Apptainer image with given Debian packages."
msgstr "Bygger en Singularity/Apptainer-avbildning med angivna Debian-paket."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:92
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<deb2docker>(1)"
msgstr "I<deb2docker>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:94
msgid "build a docker image with given Debian packages. [docker.io]"
msgstr "Bygger en Docker-avbildning med angivna Debian-paket. [docker.io]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<dep3changelog>(1)"
msgstr "I<dep3changelog>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:96
msgid "generate a changelog entry from a DEP3-style patch header."
msgstr "Skapar en post i ändringsloggen från ett patchhuvud i DEP3-format."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<dep-14-convert-git-branch-names>(1)"
msgstr "I<dep-14-convert-git-branch-names>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:98
msgid "Convert git branches to follow DEP-14."
msgstr "Konverterar gitgrenar så att de följer DEP-14."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<dget>(1)"
msgstr "I<dget>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:100
msgid ""
"Downloads Debian source and binary packages. Point at a .changes or .dsc to "
"download all references files. Specify a package name to download it from "
"the configured apt repository. [wget | curl]"
msgstr ""
"Hämtar Debian-käll- och binärpaket. Ange en .changes- eller .dsc-fil för att"
" hämta alla filer som den hänvisar till. Ange ett paketnamn för att hämta "
"det från det konfigurerade apt-arkivet. [wget | curl]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<diff2patches>(1)"
msgstr "I<diff2patches>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:102
msgid ""
"extracts patches from a .diff.gz file placing them under debian/ or, if "
"present, debian/patches. [patchutils]"
msgstr ""
"Extraherar patchar ur en .diff.gz-fil och placerar dem under debian/ eller, "
"om katalogen finns, debian/patches. [patchutils]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<dpkg-depcheck, dpkg-genbuilddeps>(1)"
msgstr "I<dpkg-depcheck, dpkg-genbuilddeps>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:104
msgid ""
"Runs a specified command (such as debian/rules build) or dpkg-buildpackage, "
"respectively, to determine the packages used during the build process.  This"
" information can be helpful when trying to determine the packages needed in "
"the Build-Depends etc. lines in the debian/control file. [build-essential, "
"strace]"
msgstr ""
"Kör ett angivet kommando, till exempel debian/rules build, respektive dpkg-"
"buildpackage för att fastställa paketen som används under bygget. "
"Informationen kan hjälpa till att avgöra vilka paket som behövs på raderna "
"Build-Depends med mera i debian/control. [build-essential, strace]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<dscextract>(1)"
msgstr "I<dscextract>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:106
msgid "extract a single file from a Debian source package. [patchutils]"
msgstr "extrahera en enskild fil från ett Debian-källpaket. [patchutils]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<dscverify>(1)"
msgstr "I<dscverify>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:108
msgid ""
"check the signature and MD5 sums of a dsc file against the most current "
"Debian keyring on your system. [gnupg, debian-keyring, debian-tag2upload-"
"keyring]"
msgstr ""
"Kontrollerar signaturen och MD5-kontrollsummorna för en dsc-fil mot den "
"senaste Debian-nyckelringen på systemet. [gnupg, debian-keyring, debian-"
"tag2upload-keyring]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<edit-patch>(1)"
msgstr "I<edit-patch>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:110
msgid "add/edit a patch for a source package and commit the changes. [quilt]"
msgstr ""
"Lägger till eller redigerar en patch för ett källpaket och checkar in "
"ändringarna. [quilt]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<getbuildlog>(1)"
msgstr "I<getbuildlog>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:112
msgid "download package build logs from Debian auto-builders. [wget | curl]"
msgstr ""
"Hämtar paketens byggloggar från Debians automatiska byggare. [wget | curl]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:112
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<grep-excuses>(1)"
msgstr "I<grep-excuses>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:114
msgid ""
"grep britney's excuses to find out what is happening to your packages. "
"[libdbd-pg-perl, libterm-size-perl, libyaml-libyaml-perl, wget, w3m]"
msgstr ""
"Söker igenom Britneys förklaringar för att ta reda på vad som händer med "
"paketen. [libdbd-pg-perl, libterm-size-perl, libyaml-libyaml-perl, wget, "
"w3m]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<hardening-check>(1)"
msgstr "I<hardening-check>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:116
msgid "report the hardening characteristics of a set of binaries."
msgstr "Rapporterar skyddsegenskaperna hos en uppsättning binärer."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<list-unreleased>(1)"
msgstr "I<list-unreleased>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:118
msgid "searches for packages marked UNRELEASED in their changelog."
msgstr ""
"Söker efter paket som är markerade som UNRELEASED i sina ändringsloggar."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<ltnu (Long Time No Upload)>(1)"
msgstr "I<ltnu (Länge sedan senaste uppladdningen)>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:120
msgid ""
"List all uploads of packages by the given uploader or maintainer and display"
" them ordered by the last upload of that package, oldest uploads first."
msgstr ""
"Listar alla paketuppladdningar av den angivna uppladdaren eller "
"underhållaren och visar dem ordnade efter paketets senaste uppladdning, med "
"de äldsta först."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<manpage-alert>(1)"
msgstr "I<manpage-alert>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:122
msgid "locate binaries without corresponding manpages. [man-db]"
msgstr "Hittar binärfiler utan motsvarande manualsidor. [man-db]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<mass-bug>(1)"
msgstr "I<mass-bug>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:124
msgid "mass-file bug reports. [bsd-mailx | mailx]"
msgstr "Massregistrerar felrapporter. [bsd-mailx | mailx]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<mergechanges>(1)"
msgstr "I<mergechanges>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:126
msgid ""
"merge .changes files from the same release but built on different "
"architectures."
msgstr ""
"Slår samman .changes-filer från samma utgåva, byggda för olika arkitekturer."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<mk-build-deps>(1)"
msgstr "I<mk-build-deps>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:128
msgid ""
"Given a package name and/or control file, generate a binary package which "
"may be installed to satisfy the build-dependencies of the given package. "
"[equivs]"
msgstr ""
"Utifrån ett paketnamn och/eller en kontrollfil skapas ett binärpaket som kan"
" installeras för att uppfylla byggberoendena för det angivna paketet. "
"[equivs]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:128
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<mk-origtargz>(1)"
msgstr "I<mk-origtargz>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:130
msgid ""
"Rename upstream tarball, optionally changing the compression and removing "
"unwanted files. [libfile-which-perl, unzip, xz-utils, file]"
msgstr ""
"Byter namn på ett uppströms tararkiv, ändrar vid behov komprimeringen och "
"tar bort oönskade filer. [libfile-which-perl, unzip, xz-utils, file]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<namecheck>(1)"
msgstr "I<namecheck>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:132
msgid "Check project names are not already taken."
msgstr "Kontrollera att projektnamnen inte redan är upptagna."

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<nmudiff>(1)"
msgstr "I<nmudiff>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:134
msgid ""
"prepare a diff of this version (presumably an NMU against the previously "
"released version (as per the changelog) and submit the diff to the BTS. "
"[patchutils, mutt]"
msgstr ""
"Förbereder en diff av denna version, förmodligen en NMU jämfört med den "
"tidigare utgivna versionen enligt ändringsloggen, och skickar diffen till "
"BTS. [patchutils, mutt]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<origtargz>(1)"
msgstr "I<origtargz>(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:136
msgid ""
"fetch the orig tarball of a Debian package from various sources, and unpack "
"it. [pristine-tar, pristine-lfs]"
msgstr ""
"Hämtar uppströms tararkivet för ett Debian-paket från olika källor och "
"packar upp det. [pristine-tar, pristine-lfs]"

#. type: IP
#: ../doc/devscripts.7:136
#, no-wrap
